WEBVTT

1
00:00:01,697 --> 00:00:03,177
(radio tuning)

2
00:00:03,351 --> 00:00:04,743
(DJ) <i>...ninth inning</i>
<i>and a walk-off home run.</i>

3
00:00:04,917 --> 00:00:07,137
<i>Game 3 of the series</i>
<i>is this coming Tuesday.</i>

4
00:00:07,311 --> 00:00:08,747
<i>Now for a quick look</i>
<i>at the weather.</i>

5
00:00:08,921 --> 00:00:10,749
<i>It was another hot one today </i>
<i>here in Dylan.</i>

6
00:00:10,923 --> 00:00:12,795
<i>But it’s looking like another </i>
<i>beautiful evening tonight,</i>

7
00:00:12,969 --> 00:00:16,364
<i>with an overnight low of 71°.</i>

8
00:00:16,538 --> 00:00:17,887
<i>All right, party people,</i>

9
00:00:18,061 --> 00:00:19,497
<i>summer’s now</i>
<i>officially dead ahead</i>

10
00:00:19,671 --> 00:00:21,151
<i>with the annual rodeo</i>
<i>coming up next weekend.</i>

11
00:00:21,325 --> 00:00:23,327
<i>Tickets still available </i>
<i>at the fairgrounds box office.</i>

12
00:00:23,501 --> 00:00:25,155
<i>But keep it right here</i>
<i>for a chance to win</i>

13
00:00:25,329 --> 00:00:27,157
<i>a pair of tickets</i>
<i>in the next hour.</i>

14
00:00:27,331 --> 00:00:30,291
<i>Until then, here’s </i>
<i>the latest from The Killers.</i>

15
00:00:30,465 --> 00:00:32,162
<i>Will this be</i>
<i>the song of the summer?</i>

16
00:00:32,336 --> 00:00:34,034
<i>Stay tuned and stay cool.</i>

17
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:36,079
("When You Were Young" playing)

18
00:00:36,253 --> 00:00:38,038
♪ <i>You sit there</i>
<i>In your heartache</i> ♪

19
00:00:38,212 --> 00:00:41,519
♪ <i>Waiting on</i>
<i>Some beautiful boy to</i> ♪

20
00:00:41,693 --> 00:00:45,132
♪ <i>To save you</i>
<i>From your old ways</i> ♪

21
00:00:45,306 --> 00:00:46,611
♪ <i>You play forgiveness</i> ♪

22
00:00:46,785 --> 00:00:48,483
♪ <i>Watch it now</i>
<i>Here he comes</i> ♪

23
00:00:48,657 --> 00:00:51,921
♪ <i>He doesn’t look a thing</i>
<i>Like Jesus</i> ♪

24
00:00:52,095 --> 00:00:54,402
♪ <i>But he talks</i>
<i>Like a gentleman</i> ♪

25
00:00:54,576 --> 00:01:00,103
♪ <i>Like you imagined</i>
<i>When you were young</i> ♪

26
00:01:03,672 --> 00:01:05,891
(Jonah) I’m on empty.
I got to fill up, right?

27
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:07,141
(man speaking indistinctly)

28
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:09,721
(Morgan) I want some, uh...
some of those salty straws.

29
00:01:09,895 --> 00:01:11,723
You want what?
(Jenny chuckles)

30
00:01:12,855 --> 00:01:15,727
So who’s gonna buy
the beer tonight?

31
00:01:15,901 --> 00:01:16,859
Oh, not me.

32
00:01:17,033 --> 00:01:18,469
Not it! Ha!

33
00:01:18,643 --> 00:01:21,820
Okay, I guess
I’ll give it a try.

34
00:01:21,994 --> 00:01:23,344
(Jenny) You’re gonna
do great, babe.

35
00:01:23,518 --> 00:01:25,085
The glasses...
They make you look mature.

36
00:01:25,259 --> 00:01:27,217
All right. I’ll be quick.
(Morgan) Jonah, hold up.

37
00:01:27,391 --> 00:01:29,393
I need to pee anyway,
so I’ll come with you.

38
00:01:32,483 --> 00:01:35,834
(song fades)
♪ <i>When you were young</i> ♪

39
00:01:36,008 --> 00:01:37,009
Thanks.
(softly) Yep.

40
00:01:37,923 --> 00:01:39,925
(billing machine beeping)

41
00:01:49,892 --> 00:01:53,896
("Fast Blood" playing)

42
00:02:09,781 --> 00:02:12,741
(song continues playing)

43
00:02:12,915 --> 00:02:14,743
(indistinct chattering)

44
00:02:14,917 --> 00:02:18,007
♪ <i>Good night</i>
<i>It’s stroke time</i> ♪

45
00:02:19,661 --> 00:02:21,967
♪ <i>Let’s get paralyzed</i> ♪

46
00:02:23,186 --> 00:02:25,841
♪ <i>Down both sides</i> ♪

47
00:02:26,015 --> 00:02:27,930
(song continues playing)
I agree.

48
00:02:28,104 --> 00:02:29,323
Have a shot.
No, thank you.

49
00:02:29,497 --> 00:02:31,847
Come on,
don’t be such a bore.

50
00:02:32,021 --> 00:02:34,937
Well, that’s my job.
I’m the designated bore tonight.

51
00:02:35,111 --> 00:02:37,940
All right. I guess I’ll just have
to have fun all by my lonesome.

52
00:02:38,114 --> 00:02:41,161
What are you saying?
I’m only fun if I’m drunk?

53
00:02:41,335 --> 00:02:43,032
Of course you’re fun.

54
00:02:43,206 --> 00:02:46,296
Just, you know... drunk Morgan
is my favorite Morgan.

55
00:02:47,428 --> 00:02:49,212
Chris Grant! Chris Grant!

56
00:02:49,386 --> 00:02:51,345
We need our champion back here!
(girl) Come on, Jenny!

57
00:02:51,519 --> 00:02:53,085
(Hank) We need you!
(girl clapping) Come on, Jenny!

58
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,044
(Chris)
Yo, Hank, we’re coming.

59
00:02:55,218 --> 00:02:57,351
You have to come.
I need you. I’m right behind you on that.

60
00:02:57,525 --> 00:02:58,395
Come on!

61
00:02:58,569 --> 00:03:00,310
(Chris) Yo! Hey! Rack it up!

62
00:03:00,484 --> 00:03:03,357
How did we both end up
with our exact opposites?

63
00:03:04,314 --> 00:03:05,663
(people cheering)

64
00:03:05,837 --> 00:03:07,839
Come on! Come on.

65
00:03:08,013 --> 00:03:09,189
Oh, shoot!

66
00:03:10,886 --> 00:03:12,061
Hey, Jonah.

67
00:03:12,844 --> 00:03:14,672
Um...

68
00:03:14,846 --> 00:03:17,371
My sister has it in her head
that tonight’s

69
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:19,938
the night for...

70
00:03:20,112 --> 00:03:21,636
Oh, no. (chuckles)

71
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:24,378
I... I have no intention
of doing that tonight.

72
00:03:24,552 --> 00:03:26,031
You have my word.

73
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,903
Thank you. (chuckles)
(Chris) Morgan!

74
00:03:28,077 --> 00:03:29,165
Come on!
You’re up!

75
00:03:29,339 --> 00:03:31,080
Your shot!
Hey, sis!

76
00:03:31,254 --> 00:03:32,560
Come on!

77
00:03:33,778 --> 00:03:35,867
I’m just not in the mood
to drink tonight.

78
00:03:36,041 --> 00:03:38,435
Me neither. It’s Pepsi.

79
00:03:38,609 --> 00:03:40,524
Oh, thank you. (chuckles)

80
00:03:42,874 --> 00:03:44,789
He didn’t mean
what he said.

81
00:03:44,963 --> 00:03:47,531
He’s drunk.
You know how he gets.

82
00:03:47,705 --> 00:03:49,794
Mmm. He’s probably right.

83
00:03:51,753 --> 00:03:53,320
He’s not.

84
00:03:53,494 --> 00:03:55,452
There’s no version of you
that’s boring.

85
00:04:03,547 --> 00:04:04,679
I’m pregnant.

86
00:04:10,075 --> 00:04:11,860
(fireworks exploding)

87
00:04:12,034 --> 00:04:14,079
(people exclaiming)

88
00:04:53,945 --> 00:04:55,338
(exhales)

89
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,214
(Jonah) All right, buddy.
Was that fun?

90
00:05:02,389 --> 00:05:03,999
(Jenny)
Oh, there’s our little guy.

91
00:05:04,173 --> 00:05:06,044
Okay.

92
00:05:06,218 --> 00:05:08,743
Was that fun?
Yeah, he’s good.

93
00:05:08,917 --> 00:05:10,353
(car door closes)
(Jonah) You okay?

94
00:05:10,527 --> 00:05:12,660
(Jenny) Do you want to go
and see your auntie?

95
00:05:12,834 --> 00:05:14,314
She’s the birthday girl.

96
00:05:15,184 --> 00:05:16,403
(Jonah) Okay.

97
00:05:16,577 --> 00:05:17,882
(Jenny) Look who it is!

98
00:05:18,056 --> 00:05:20,798
Oh, my gosh. Hi.
Get out of there!

99
00:05:20,972 --> 00:05:22,234
Stop doing dishes
on your birthday.

100
00:05:22,409 --> 00:05:24,802
Take the baby.
Who’s my favorite nephew?

101
00:05:24,976 --> 00:05:26,717
Hi.

102
00:05:26,891 --> 00:05:28,676
You know, it’s bad enough you
make your own cake every year.

103
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:31,374
Well, someone else could learn
how to do it, in theory.

104
00:05:31,548 --> 00:05:34,029
I’m just sayin’... Stop judging,
Mother Morgan. Get out of here.

105
00:05:34,203 --> 00:05:35,506
I guess I raised you right.

106
00:05:35,530 --> 00:05:37,256
I just never thought of you
as a dish-doing kind of gal.

107
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,555
(Jenny) Mm-hmm.

108
00:05:38,729 --> 00:05:40,252
Okay, grill’s fixed.
Yeah? Thank you.

109
00:05:40,427 --> 00:05:41,341
Ready when you are.

110
00:05:41,515 --> 00:05:42,646
Thank you.
Look who I have!

111
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:44,213
Hi! Hey, little fella.
Hello!

112
00:05:44,387 --> 00:05:45,780
You ready to party?
Always.

113
00:05:45,954 --> 00:05:47,129
Of course you are.
Always.

114
00:05:47,303 --> 00:05:48,652
Oh, you’re the sweetest guy.

115
00:05:48,826 --> 00:05:50,785
Hi there.
Hey. Hi.

116
00:05:50,959 --> 00:05:52,613
We’re just waiting on Clara.
She’s supposed to be home by 5:00.

117
00:05:52,787 --> 00:05:55,920
I’m sure her rehearsal
just ran late. Want a beer?

118
00:05:56,094 --> 00:05:57,748
No. No, thank you.

119
00:05:57,922 --> 00:06:00,185
It’s your birthday, relax.
I know, I’m very relaxed.

120
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,579
Jen?
Yes, please. Thank you.

121
00:06:02,753 --> 00:06:04,364
Pumping and dumping.
(chuckles)

122
00:06:06,104 --> 00:06:08,019
(door hinge squeaks)
Hey.

123
00:06:08,803 --> 00:06:10,152
Hey.
What’s up, bud?

124
00:06:10,326 --> 00:06:11,240
What’s up, man?

125
00:06:11,414 --> 00:06:12,894
Beer?
Ah, I’m good.

126
00:06:13,068 --> 00:06:14,069
You need some help?

127
00:06:14,243 --> 00:06:15,679
Uh, do you want to dry?
Yeah.

128
00:06:15,853 --> 00:06:17,986
Oh, actually,
I have a job for one of you,

129
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:20,902
which is that this guy
just unleashed...

130
00:06:21,076 --> 00:06:22,425
(Jenny) Oh!
...something incredible

131
00:06:22,599 --> 00:06:23,557
into his diaper.

132
00:06:23,731 --> 00:06:25,646
I got it. Come here.

133
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,909
Ooh, that is stinky, dude!
Aww...

134
00:06:28,083 --> 00:06:29,650
Thanks, Daddy.
Be right back.

135
00:06:29,824 --> 00:06:32,392
Okay, if Clara’s not back soon,
we start without her.

136
00:06:32,566 --> 00:06:34,176
Yeah, right.

137
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:36,961
Sounded good, right?
Oh, my God, yes!

138
00:06:37,135 --> 00:06:39,573
Laying down the law.
I love it, babe.

139
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,879
(door hinge squeaking)

140
00:06:43,054 --> 00:06:44,534
Oh, I hate that door.

141
00:06:45,927 --> 00:06:47,276
So, hey.

142
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:48,495
Hey.

143
00:06:50,018 --> 00:06:51,759
Jonah and I decided
to get married.

144
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:54,414
He proposed?

145
00:06:54,588 --> 00:06:57,852
Uh, well, I mean,
no, not exactly. It was...

146
00:06:58,026 --> 00:07:00,594
It was... a discussion.

147
00:07:00,768 --> 00:07:02,857
It makes sense for it
to be our next move.

148
00:07:03,031 --> 00:07:06,077
Well, that’s romantic.

149
00:07:07,905 --> 00:07:11,039
Yeah. I’ll do that.
Okay.

150
00:07:11,213 --> 00:07:12,910
I’m sorry,
your proposal was better?

151
00:07:13,084 --> 00:07:14,434
No, but that’s
what I’m saying.

152
00:07:14,608 --> 00:07:16,871
Except you knew this guy
in high school

153
00:07:17,045 --> 00:07:19,047
and then you didn’t see him
for a gazillion years

154
00:07:19,221 --> 00:07:22,703
then you slept together once
at his dad’s funeral?

155
00:07:22,877 --> 00:07:24,139
We used to date.

156
00:07:24,313 --> 00:07:25,923
I mean, we’ve like... (scoffs)

157
00:07:26,097 --> 00:07:28,012
We’ve known each other forever.

158
00:07:28,186 --> 00:07:30,275
You dated for a month
all those years ago.

159
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,842
I mean, it’s just...
(Jenny) What?

160
00:07:32,974 --> 00:07:34,802
Morgan,
we have a baby together.

161
00:07:34,976 --> 00:07:37,065
Isn’t that the same reason
that you and Chris got married?

162
00:07:37,892 --> 00:07:39,241
I mean...

163
00:07:39,415 --> 00:07:41,199
can’t you just
be happy for me?

164
00:07:42,592 --> 00:07:43,637
I’m sorry.

165
00:07:43,811 --> 00:07:46,640
Yes. Of course.
Of course I am.

166
00:07:46,814 --> 00:07:49,294
Congratulations. This is...
It’s really exciting.

167
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:51,166
Thank you.

168
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,603
Okay.
I’ll be a good maid of honor.

169
00:07:54,648 --> 00:07:56,127
Promise.
(chuckles)

170
00:07:57,433 --> 00:07:59,653
Where is Clara?

171
00:07:59,827 --> 00:08:01,829
(Clara singing along to stereo)
♪ <i>Wish I could do.. What I’m told</i> ♪

172
00:08:02,003 --> 00:08:03,787
♪ <i>Aw, no</i> ♪

173
00:08:03,961 --> 00:08:06,137
♪ <i>Dad’s on the phone</i>
<i>And he’s lecturing me</i> ♪

174
00:08:06,311 --> 00:08:09,489
♪ <i>’Bout a girl that he met</i>
<i>Back when he was 19</i> ♪

175
00:08:09,663 --> 00:08:13,231
♪ <i>It’s never gonna work ’cause </i>
<i>The puzzle won’t piece...</i> ♪

176
00:08:13,405 --> 00:08:14,624
(cell phone ringing)

177
00:08:14,798 --> 00:08:16,800
What? That’s the best part.
Come on.

178
00:08:18,106 --> 00:08:19,586
(music continues playing
over car stereo)

179
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,978
(continues singing along)
♪ <i>Son of a gun</i> ♪

180
00:08:21,152 --> 00:08:22,980
♪ <i>But I know that he’s right</i>♪

181
00:08:23,154 --> 00:08:25,156
♪ <i>’Cause the girl that I love </i>
<i>Never treated me right</i> ♪

182
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:28,290
♪ <i>Writing’s on the wall</i>
<i>I pretend I can’t read</i> ♪

183
00:08:28,464 --> 00:08:30,814
Shit. Don’t turn around, Clara.

184
00:08:30,988 --> 00:08:32,990
♪ <i>You’re forgetting me</i> ♪

185
00:08:33,164 --> 00:08:34,818
♪ <i>Losing my patience</i> ♪

186
00:08:35,993 --> 00:08:38,692
♪ <i>Confusing the waitress</i> ♪
Hmm.

187
00:08:38,866 --> 00:08:41,738
♪ <i>She said, "Honey</i>
<i>You’ll be all right"</i> ♪ (grunting)

188
00:08:41,912 --> 00:08:44,480
♪ <i>But she gets paid</i>
<i>To be nice</i>♪

189
00:08:44,654 --> 00:08:48,745
♪ <i>Ah, hell, Dad’s on the phone </i>
<i>And he’s lecturing me</i> ♪

190
00:08:48,919 --> 00:08:52,009
♪ <i>’Bout a girl that he met</i>
<i>Back when he was 19</i> ♪

191
00:08:52,183 --> 00:08:57,275
♪ <i>It’s never gonna work ’cause </i>
<i>The puzzle won’t piece...</i> ♪

192
00:08:57,449 --> 00:08:58,842
(Miller) Hey, Clara.

193
00:08:59,016 --> 00:09:00,409
(song stops playing)
You burying bodies out here?

194
00:09:00,583 --> 00:09:02,280
That’s exactly
what I’m doing, yeah.

195
00:09:02,454 --> 00:09:03,586
Come here a sec.

196
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,501
Look, I stopped
to offer you a ride,

197
00:09:05,675 --> 00:09:07,895
not get involved in whatever
shady shit you’re up to.

198
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,897
(grunting)

199
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:12,682
What are you doing?
I’ll show you. Come here.

200
00:09:12,856 --> 00:09:15,119
Look, it’s my mom’s birthday
and I’m already running late.

201
00:09:15,293 --> 00:09:18,166
Okay, then hurry up.
Before I get caught.

202
00:09:20,951 --> 00:09:22,823
(chuckles)

203
00:09:25,608 --> 00:09:29,003
God. These shoes
aren’t meant for this.

204
00:09:30,308 --> 00:09:32,484
Those aren’t shoes.

205
00:09:32,659 --> 00:09:34,312
Stealing the city limit sign?

206
00:09:34,486 --> 00:09:35,836
(grunts)

207
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:37,359
Nope, just moving it.
(groans)

208
00:09:37,533 --> 00:09:38,665
Can you grab that end?
(sighs)

209
00:09:38,839 --> 00:09:39,970
Giving you a ride
is one thing,

210
00:09:40,144 --> 00:09:41,319
being your accomplice
is another.

211
00:09:41,493 --> 00:09:42,538
(sighs)

212
00:09:43,539 --> 00:09:44,584
(sign clanks)

213
00:09:46,063 --> 00:09:48,065
(cattle lowing)
(sighs)

214
00:09:53,549 --> 00:09:55,203
Why are we doing this again?

215
00:09:55,377 --> 00:09:58,467
Okay, so my gramps,
he can’t get out much.

216
00:09:58,641 --> 00:09:59,686
And Roman’s Pizza
doesn’t deliver

217
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:01,601
outside of city limits,
so...

218
00:10:01,775 --> 00:10:03,298
I’ve been coming out here
every day

219
00:10:03,472 --> 00:10:05,517
moving this sign
little by little where no one notices.

220
00:10:05,692 --> 00:10:07,476
Breaking the law for pizza?

221
00:10:08,651 --> 00:10:11,088
It’s really good pizza.
(chuckles)

222
00:10:11,262 --> 00:10:13,830
Shit.
You okay? Oh.

223
00:10:14,004 --> 00:10:15,571
I’ll buy you some new ones.

224
00:10:25,537 --> 00:10:27,104
(sighs)

225
00:10:28,105 --> 00:10:29,454
All right, perfect.

226
00:10:31,718 --> 00:10:33,720
I’ll take that ride now.

227
00:10:33,894 --> 00:10:36,636
(pop song playing over radio)

228
00:10:44,426 --> 00:10:45,819
(Miller) Whoa, all A’s?

229
00:10:45,993 --> 00:10:47,951
Do you study a lot
or does it come natural?

230
00:10:48,125 --> 00:10:49,997
A little bit of both.

231
00:10:51,607 --> 00:10:55,480
You always this nosy?
Sorry, only child syndrome.

232
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:57,047
Yeah. I’m an only child.

233
00:10:57,221 --> 00:10:59,093
You don’t see me rifling
through your pockets.

234
00:10:59,267 --> 00:11:01,269
Do you want to rifle
through my pockets?

235
00:11:04,446 --> 00:11:07,318
My mom would flip if she knew
how serious I was about acting.

236
00:11:07,492 --> 00:11:09,843
She thinks I’m only
gonna apply to State.

237
00:11:12,149 --> 00:11:13,411
You applied anywhere?

238
00:11:13,585 --> 00:11:16,632
Uh, my gramps is insisting
I apply to UNCSA.

239
00:11:16,806 --> 00:11:19,243
But 100K in student loan debt
for a film degree

240
00:11:19,417 --> 00:11:21,985
is, like,
horror-movie scary, so...

241
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:24,640
UNCSA is my first pick
for drama school.

242
00:11:24,814 --> 00:11:26,033
Yeah?

243
00:11:26,207 --> 00:11:27,861
Yeah, you want to go
to film school there?

244
00:11:28,035 --> 00:11:30,341
Uh...
(cell phone buzzes)

245
00:11:32,474 --> 00:11:34,694
Uh, hey, babe. Um...

246
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:38,349
Nah, I was just
on a walk home

247
00:11:38,523 --> 00:11:40,308
and I got hot
so I caught a ride.

248
00:11:42,658 --> 00:11:44,268
Just some dude, I don’t know.

249
00:11:45,661 --> 00:11:47,271
Yeah, yeah,
I’ll talk to you later.

250
00:11:47,445 --> 00:11:49,317
Okay. Bye.

251
00:11:51,885 --> 00:11:53,277
"Just some dude"?

252
00:11:53,451 --> 00:11:55,279
Now who’s being nosy?

253
00:11:57,542 --> 00:11:58,979
(horse neighs)

254
00:11:59,153 --> 00:12:00,545
(goat bleating)

255
00:12:22,350 --> 00:12:25,570
Not what you were expecting?
No, I was just...

256
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,094
My wallet’s inside.

257
00:12:27,268 --> 00:12:29,400
You know, to pay for
those things you call shoes.

258
00:12:31,185 --> 00:12:33,622
So, do you always
lie to your girlfriend?

259
00:12:33,796 --> 00:12:35,667
(chuckles)

260
00:12:35,842 --> 00:12:36,973
Well, if it saves me

261
00:12:37,147 --> 00:12:39,759
from a three-hour
interrogation, yeah.

262
00:12:39,933 --> 00:12:41,717
Sounds like a super

263
00:12:41,891 --> 00:12:43,806
healthy relationship.

264
00:12:48,724 --> 00:12:50,030
That’s Gramps.

265
00:12:50,204 --> 00:12:51,727
Hmm.

266
00:12:59,996 --> 00:13:00,997
(grunts)

267
00:13:14,010 --> 00:13:15,011
(drawer thuds)

268
00:13:17,971 --> 00:13:19,015
Okay, look.

269
00:13:19,189 --> 00:13:20,060
If those cost
more than ten bucks,

270
00:13:20,234 --> 00:13:21,235
you’ve been ripped off.

271
00:13:22,584 --> 00:13:23,846
I don’t--

272
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:25,413
Okay. I’ve got a job.
Take the money.

273
00:13:25,587 --> 00:13:27,154
I don’t actually expect you--

274
00:13:36,554 --> 00:13:38,556
Pleasure doing business
with you.

275
00:13:42,909 --> 00:13:45,172
Guess you weren’t kidding
about film school.

276
00:13:45,346 --> 00:13:47,000
Why would I kid about that?

277
00:13:47,739 --> 00:13:48,958
I don’t know.

278
00:13:49,132 --> 00:13:50,177
Me wanting to be an actress

279
00:13:50,351 --> 00:13:52,440
can sound kind of silly
sometimes.

280
00:13:53,397 --> 00:13:54,834
I don’t think so.

281
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:57,053
(cell phone buzzing)

282
00:14:00,796 --> 00:14:03,625
I think that’s
this dude’s cue to leave.

283
00:14:10,371 --> 00:14:11,981
Oh, hey, Gramps.
You take your meds?

284
00:14:12,155 --> 00:14:15,463
Every damn day since your
grandma skipped out on me.

285
00:14:15,637 --> 00:14:18,074
Yeah, Grandma didn’t skip town.
She died of a heart attack.

286
00:14:18,248 --> 00:14:19,728
Yeah, well,
either way, she left me

287
00:14:19,902 --> 00:14:21,164
and I’ll never
forgive her for it.

288
00:14:21,338 --> 00:14:22,600
Mmm...

289
00:14:24,341 --> 00:14:26,343
Hey, now come on!
Those don’t grow on trees!

290
00:14:26,517 --> 00:14:28,345
Yeah, and neither do lungs.
So...

291
00:14:29,781 --> 00:14:32,610
Did I not teach you manners?
Introduce me, damn it.

292
00:14:32,784 --> 00:14:33,785
Yeah, um...

293
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,831
Oh, uh... Hi. Clara.
This is...

294
00:14:36,005 --> 00:14:37,746
Clara,
a friend from school.

295
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,617
Clara, this is
my very grumpy gramps.

296
00:14:39,791 --> 00:14:41,402
Hi.Don’t listen to him.

297
00:14:41,576 --> 00:14:43,883
Who is this? Who are you?

298
00:14:44,057 --> 00:14:46,711
That’s Charlie.
Charles if he misbehaves.

299
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,104
Clara, huh?

300
00:14:48,278 --> 00:14:50,237
Clara... Clara Grant, hmm?

301
00:14:51,455 --> 00:14:52,848
Yeah. How did you know?

302
00:14:53,022 --> 00:14:54,415
Hey, Clara Grant,
would you tell my grandson

303
00:14:54,589 --> 00:14:56,286
that if he breaks
another one of my cigarettes,

304
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,680
I’m rescinding his inheritance?
(Clara and Miller chuckle)

305
00:14:58,854 --> 00:15:00,334
Yeah, go ahead.

306
00:15:00,508 --> 00:15:02,510
You said the only thing
you have of any value is air.

307
00:15:02,684 --> 00:15:04,816
Yeah, air which
you will not be inheriting.

308
00:15:04,991 --> 00:15:07,254
Mmm...
I get my charm from him.

309
00:15:07,428 --> 00:15:08,820
(chuckles)

310
00:15:08,995 --> 00:15:10,910
Clara, would you like to hear
some Miller stories?

311
00:15:11,084 --> 00:15:12,259
I got plenty of them.

312
00:15:12,433 --> 00:15:14,348
(laughs) Absolutely.
Well, that’s--

313
00:15:14,522 --> 00:15:16,089
(Gramps) Once when Miller
was six years old,

314
00:15:16,263 --> 00:15:18,091
he pooped his pants
in a grocery store

315
00:15:18,265 --> 00:15:20,528
because the automatic flushers
on the public toilets terrified him.

316
00:15:20,702 --> 00:15:21,833
Okay. Let’s go, come on.

317
00:15:22,008 --> 00:15:22,922
(Gramps) Wait, wait,
I got another one!

318
00:15:23,096 --> 00:15:25,011
When he was 15--
I got video--

319
00:15:25,185 --> 00:15:27,143
We went to a school play,
wasn’t it?

320
00:15:27,317 --> 00:15:28,928
Remember that?
Oh, no. Okay.

321
00:15:29,102 --> 00:15:30,581
Thank you, Gramps. Let’s go.
No, please, I want to see.

322
00:15:30,755 --> 00:15:32,453
(Gramps) All right,
you come back any time!

323
00:15:32,627 --> 00:15:34,107
Bye! What play?

324
00:15:34,281 --> 00:15:35,978
Okay, don’t mind him.
He’s old and confused.

325
00:15:36,152 --> 00:15:39,416
No, I don’t know,
once you finish your city limits mission,

326
00:15:39,590 --> 00:15:41,331
I might just have to order
a pepperoni-and-pineapple

327
00:15:41,505 --> 00:15:42,550
and get Gramps to tell me

328
00:15:42,724 --> 00:15:43,855
embarrassing
Miller Adams stories.

329
00:15:44,030 --> 00:15:46,510
Pineapple on pizza?
Mm-hmm...

330
00:15:46,684 --> 00:15:48,164
You’re not welcome here.

331
00:15:49,339 --> 00:15:50,601
(Clara chuckles)
(Miller chuckles)

332
00:15:52,168 --> 00:15:55,389
("Just You" playing)

333
00:15:57,173 --> 00:15:59,175
You can go
call your girlfriend now.

334
00:16:01,873 --> 00:16:02,962
See you at school, Clara.

335
00:16:04,311 --> 00:16:06,835
♪ <i>Sun’s set</i>♪

336
00:16:07,009 --> 00:16:10,578
♪ <i>I’ve waited for you</i>
<i>All day</i> ♪ (phone chimes)

337
00:16:11,883 --> 00:16:15,975
♪ <i>I’ve waited for you</i>
<i>All day</i> ♪

338
00:16:16,149 --> 00:16:18,238
♪ <i>My love</i> ♪

339
00:16:21,328 --> 00:16:24,331
(singer vocalizing)

340
00:16:30,293 --> 00:16:34,036
♪ <i>Just you, just you</i>
<i>Just you, just you</i> ♪

341
00:16:34,210 --> 00:16:36,038
(song ends)

342
00:16:37,257 --> 00:16:39,520
(muffled men chattering)
Jenny.

343
00:16:39,694 --> 00:16:41,870
Just wait, okay?
It’s coming together.

344
00:16:42,044 --> 00:16:44,742
(cell phone ringing)
Ah!

345
00:16:44,916 --> 00:16:46,527
Hey, Clare Bear.

346
00:16:46,701 --> 00:16:48,268
What’s up? Your mom tried
calling you. Where are you?

347
00:16:48,442 --> 00:16:50,705
Yeah. Sorry, I know--
rehearsal ran long.

348
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:52,359
I’ve got to grab Lexie still.

349
00:16:52,533 --> 00:16:53,708
Am I on speaker?

350
00:16:53,882 --> 00:16:55,014
No. Of course not.

351
00:16:55,188 --> 00:16:57,016
(imperceptible)
<i>Guess who just</i>

352
00:16:57,190 --> 00:16:58,365
spent the last half hour

353
00:16:58,539 --> 00:16:59,888
with the coolest guy in school.

354
00:17:00,062 --> 00:17:01,324
Oh, my God.

355
00:17:01,498 --> 00:17:03,152
Really?
(mouths)

356
00:17:03,326 --> 00:17:06,025
Mm-hmm. I helped him move
a city limits sign-- don’t ask.

357
00:17:06,199 --> 00:17:08,897
And I gave him a ride home.
We hung out in his bedroom.

358
00:17:09,071 --> 00:17:11,030
<i>And now he’s following me.</i>
(mouths) Bedroom!

359
00:17:11,204 --> 00:17:13,945
That’s so exciting.
(Clara) <i>Yeah.</i>

360
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:15,382
Should I follow him back?

361
00:17:15,556 --> 00:17:17,123
<i>I mean, he told his girlfriend</i>

362
00:17:17,297 --> 00:17:18,907
<i>that "some dude"</i>
<i>gave him a ride home, so...</i>

363
00:17:19,081 --> 00:17:20,822
clearly they’ve got
a messed-up thing going on.

364
00:17:20,996 --> 00:17:22,606
Wait, he has a girlfriend?
(Clara) <i>Yeah.</i>

365
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,608
Yeah, she graduated last year.

366
00:17:24,782 --> 00:17:27,046
No, um, don’t do that.

367
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:29,744
You have to stay away,
Clare Bear. He’s taken.

368
00:17:29,918 --> 00:17:31,354
<i>Yeah, okay.</i>

369
00:17:31,528 --> 00:17:33,443
Hey, listen,
don’t tell my mom about this.

370
00:17:33,617 --> 00:17:34,966
You know how she gets.

371
00:17:35,141 --> 00:17:37,012
Yeah. No, of course I won’t.
Don’t worry.

372
00:17:37,186 --> 00:17:39,449
Okay, see you soon.
(Clara) <i>Bye.</i>

373
00:17:42,365 --> 00:17:44,889
Sometimes it scares me
how good of a liar you are.

374
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:48,632
Well... boo!
(Morgan chuckles)

375
00:17:48,806 --> 00:17:51,113
You want some?
(Morgan) Stop! No!

376
00:17:51,287 --> 00:17:52,897
(Chris) Lexie, can you hand me
some more of those chips?

377
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,290
(Lexie) Yes.
(Chris) Thanks.

378
00:17:54,464 --> 00:17:55,813
(chuckles)
(baby exclaims)

379
00:17:55,987 --> 00:17:57,250
(Clara gasps)

380
00:17:57,424 --> 00:17:59,730
(Jonah) What is that?
What is that, dude?

381
00:17:59,904 --> 00:18:02,168
(Jonah chuckles)
Lexie, phone down.

382
00:18:02,342 --> 00:18:04,170
It’s my Tinder date,
Mr. Grant.

383
00:18:04,344 --> 00:18:05,867
Don’t you have to be 18
to be on that app?

384
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:07,303
I am 18...

385
00:18:08,478 --> 00:18:09,784
on Tinder.

386
00:18:11,133 --> 00:18:12,395
So, back at it tomorrow, huh?

387
00:18:12,569 --> 00:18:15,485
Excited?
Mmm! Oh, yes. You have no idea.

388
00:18:15,659 --> 00:18:17,966
What’s tomorrow?
She’s coming back to work.

389
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:20,534
Yeah, maternity leave
is officially over.

390
00:18:20,708 --> 00:18:22,927
I feel like I figured out
that I am not cut out

391
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,407
to be a stay-at-home mom.

392
00:18:24,581 --> 00:18:25,930
That’s what I’ve realized.
(chuckles)

393
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,584
Thank you for watching Elijah.

394
00:18:27,758 --> 00:18:29,325
And don’t worry,
he’ll be in day care next week.

395
00:18:29,499 --> 00:18:32,154
Oh, my gosh, don’t be silly.
I’m so excited.

396
00:18:32,328 --> 00:18:33,677
He’s my favorite guy
to hang out with,

397
00:18:33,851 --> 00:18:35,505
right?
(Elijah coos)

398
00:18:35,679 --> 00:18:37,812
I think he looks exactly like
Clara did when she was his age.

399
00:18:37,986 --> 00:18:40,031
Exactly. Don’t you think?

400
00:18:40,206 --> 00:18:42,599
(gasps) Do you?
Are you a pretty boy?

401
00:18:42,773 --> 00:18:45,211
I think he looks
just like his gorgeous daddy.

402
00:18:45,385 --> 00:18:47,126
Right?
(Elijah coos)

403
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,605
You want cake?

404
00:18:48,779 --> 00:18:50,651
Yep, sure. I’m down for cake.

405
00:18:50,825 --> 00:18:51,826
I’ll get it!

406
00:18:56,309 --> 00:18:59,007
Oh, my God! Miller Adams
is following you?

407
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:02,576
I gave him a ride today.

408
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:05,405
(Lexie) Oh, got it.
So you were in your car

409
00:19:05,579 --> 00:19:07,102
with him alone
and you didn’t tell me.

410
00:19:07,276 --> 00:19:09,017
Can we talk about it later?
Okay, please.

411
00:19:09,191 --> 00:19:10,584
Why do I know that name?

412
00:19:10,758 --> 00:19:12,281
Miller Adams. Wait.

413
00:19:12,455 --> 00:19:13,891
Is that Hank’s kid?

414
00:19:16,894 --> 00:19:17,982
You remember Hank.

415
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,594
No.
I remember Hank.

416
00:19:20,768 --> 00:19:22,596
There’s still people
named Hank?

417
00:19:22,770 --> 00:19:24,206
He sold drugs
and went to prison.

418
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:26,426
Someone we know
was Hank’s best customer.

419
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:29,907
Wait a minute. Hank’s son
is the coolest guy in school?

420
00:19:30,081 --> 00:19:32,171
And it was just
the two of you today?

421
00:19:32,345 --> 00:19:34,695
Miller’s a student of mine.
He’s actually a really good kid.

422
00:19:34,869 --> 00:19:36,784
No offense, but you have him
for 45 minutes a day,

423
00:19:36,958 --> 00:19:38,351
and he’s on his best behavior.

424
00:19:38,525 --> 00:19:40,004
You don’t really know
what kind of kid he is.

425
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:42,659
We’re not dating anyone
whose father’s a felon.

426
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:44,661
My God, I just gave him a ride.

427
00:19:44,835 --> 00:19:46,924
Okay, relax.
Nobody’s dating anybody.

428
00:19:47,098 --> 00:19:49,971
Clara is staying away because
the boy has a girlfriend.

429
00:19:51,364 --> 00:19:52,452
(Lexie) I don’t know.
My mom always said

430
00:19:52,626 --> 00:19:54,149
that just because
there’s a goalie

431
00:19:54,323 --> 00:19:55,455
doesn’t mean
you can’t score.

432
00:19:56,586 --> 00:19:58,893
What?
Your mom always says that?

433
00:19:59,067 --> 00:20:01,417
Yeah.(both giggle)

434
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:06,422
Oh. Thank you. You can just
put those right there.

435
00:20:06,596 --> 00:20:07,597
Okay.

436
00:20:14,822 --> 00:20:15,866
What?

437
00:20:17,085 --> 00:20:18,652
Oh, my God, just say it!

438
00:20:18,826 --> 00:20:20,262
You can’t look at me like that
and not say anything.

439
00:20:20,436 --> 00:20:21,916
My being here bothers you.

440
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:23,309
Jonah.

441
00:20:23,483 --> 00:20:26,007
Just, I want things
to be okay with us.

442
00:20:26,181 --> 00:20:29,576
(sighs) Okay, should we do this?
Should we just do this now?

443
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,534
Yes! Tell me. Just say it.

444
00:20:31,708 --> 00:20:33,188
Okay.

445
00:20:33,362 --> 00:20:36,496
You graduated and you dumped
Jenny and you disappeared.

446
00:20:36,670 --> 00:20:38,933
You just left. You didn’t
give us any explanation.

447
00:20:39,107 --> 00:20:40,369
Where you were going,

448
00:20:40,543 --> 00:20:41,849
when we would hear
from you next, nothing.

449
00:20:42,023 --> 00:20:43,938
Do you have any idea
how many times I called you?

450
00:20:44,112 --> 00:20:45,722
You didn’t respond once!

451
00:20:45,896 --> 00:20:47,594
I thought we were friends.
We are.

452
00:20:47,768 --> 00:20:50,901
No, no, no. You get my sister pregnant,
move back to town,

453
00:20:51,075 --> 00:20:52,642
and I’m supposed to be,
like, fine with it,

454
00:20:52,816 --> 00:20:54,992
but it’s taking me a minute.
Okay?

455
00:20:55,166 --> 00:20:58,387
That’s fair. And I’m sorry.

456
00:20:58,561 --> 00:21:01,085
But Jenny’s so happy,

457
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,044
and you’ve really
stepped up as a dad.

458
00:21:04,219 --> 00:21:05,655
And I guess
that’s all that matters.

459
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,492
Hey, before I forget.

460
00:21:17,667 --> 00:21:18,886
Happy birthday.

461
00:21:22,193 --> 00:21:23,891
Can’t stay mad at me
forever.

462
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:29,723
Bye, guys.
Happy birthday.

463
00:21:29,897 --> 00:21:31,855
Bye, Jenny, Jonah.
You’re wobbly.

464
00:21:32,029 --> 00:21:33,901
(Chris) Do not let her drive.
Absolutely not. I got her.

465
00:21:34,075 --> 00:21:35,816
I’m just unlocking the car.
I’ll see you in the morning!

466
00:21:35,990 --> 00:21:38,253
(Jonah) I got it.
Thank you. Happy birthday. (sighs)

467
00:21:38,427 --> 00:21:40,995
(singing)
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you</i> ♪

468
00:21:41,169 --> 00:21:43,824
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you</i> ♪

469
00:21:43,998 --> 00:21:46,479
Aww, I think I might have
sabotaged my own birthday.

470
00:21:46,653 --> 00:21:47,915
What? Why?

471
00:21:48,089 --> 00:21:49,699
I feel like the Hank thing
just threw me off

472
00:21:49,873 --> 00:21:52,180
and I think we might’ve been
too hard on her. Were we?

473
00:21:52,354 --> 00:21:54,835
No! No. We have
to nip that in the bud.

474
00:21:55,009 --> 00:21:56,750
Okay. Yes.
Okay?

475
00:21:56,924 --> 00:21:59,318
Happy birthday.
Aww...

476
00:21:59,492 --> 00:22:01,711
Thank you.
I’ll do the dishes, okay?

477
00:22:03,365 --> 00:22:04,671
I already did them.

478
00:22:05,454 --> 00:22:06,368
(sighs)

479
00:22:06,542 --> 00:22:08,109
Mom.
Yeah?

480
00:22:08,283 --> 00:22:09,415
It’s that time.

481
00:22:09,589 --> 00:22:11,895
Oh, my gosh. Of course it is.Mm-hmm.

482
00:22:15,029 --> 00:22:16,726
And there we go. Yay me!

483
00:22:16,900 --> 00:22:20,077
Big one. Congratulations.
Thank you very much.

484
00:22:20,251 --> 00:22:22,253
(chuckles)
Watermelon’s the best.

485
00:22:22,428 --> 00:22:24,778
Yes, it’s the only flavor
worth the cavities.

486
00:22:24,952 --> 00:22:26,606
I’m proud of how many of these
I’ve checked off.

487
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:27,824
I know.

488
00:22:27,998 --> 00:22:30,566
"Get a phone.
Any phone is good."

489
00:22:30,740 --> 00:22:32,307
(laughs)

490
00:22:32,481 --> 00:22:34,048
I regret that one.

491
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:38,574
But you don’t like that one.
I didn’t say anything.

492
00:22:39,793 --> 00:22:42,186
Mmm, you didn’t have to.
It’s just...

493
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:43,797
the world is so hard.

494
00:22:43,971 --> 00:22:45,451
That world is even harder.

495
00:22:45,625 --> 00:22:46,843
The odds are
stacked against you.

496
00:22:47,017 --> 00:22:48,149
I think it’s smart
if you just--

497
00:22:48,323 --> 00:22:49,585
Yeah, get a degree
in something more...

498
00:22:50,238 --> 00:22:51,544
realistic.

499
00:22:51,718 --> 00:22:53,894
Just as a backup.

500
00:22:54,068 --> 00:22:55,504
But whenever
you were my age,

501
00:22:55,678 --> 00:22:57,288
didn’t you have anything
that you were, like...

502
00:22:57,463 --> 00:22:58,986
actually passionate about?

503
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:02,119
I went from raising Aunt Jenny
to being pregnant with you

504
00:23:02,293 --> 00:23:03,643
and then raising you and...

505
00:23:03,817 --> 00:23:07,211
I never had time in there
for my passions.

506
00:23:07,386 --> 00:23:10,345
Well, that’s... sad.

507
00:23:10,519 --> 00:23:11,477
I don’t know.

508
00:23:11,651 --> 00:23:12,913
I think...

509
00:23:14,131 --> 00:23:15,568
that your goal this year
should be...

510
00:23:15,742 --> 00:23:17,004
Okay.

511
00:23:17,744 --> 00:23:19,702
"Find your...

512
00:23:20,790 --> 00:23:22,705
passion!"Mm-hmm.

513
00:23:22,879 --> 00:23:24,490
(Morgan) Okay,
I have a question for you.

514
00:23:24,664 --> 00:23:26,056
Mm-hmm...

515
00:23:26,230 --> 00:23:29,495
When you think of me,
what one word comes to mind?

516
00:23:29,669 --> 00:23:31,410
Not something
like "mom" or "wife,"

517
00:23:31,584 --> 00:23:33,150
but something descriptive.

518
00:23:33,324 --> 00:23:35,109
Right now? "Overprotective."

519
00:23:35,283 --> 00:23:37,328
Overprotective?

520
00:23:37,503 --> 00:23:39,418
I didn’t say you were cruel.
I’m exactly as protective

521
00:23:39,592 --> 00:23:41,898
as I’m supposed to be.
Okay, then I’ll pick a new one.

522
00:23:42,986 --> 00:23:44,161
"Predictable."

523
00:23:44,335 --> 00:23:46,120
Predictable?

524
00:23:46,294 --> 00:23:49,166
But not in a bad way.
I prefer overprotective.

525
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:51,473
I meant, like, dependable.

526
00:23:51,647 --> 00:23:53,562
My soul is dying.
(cell phone dings)

527
00:23:53,736 --> 00:23:55,346
(chuckles)
I love my predictable,

528
00:23:55,521 --> 00:23:56,913
dependable,
overprotective mom.

529
00:23:57,087 --> 00:23:58,567
Well, good.
She’s the only one you’ve got.

530
00:23:58,741 --> 00:24:00,439
Um...

531
00:24:00,613 --> 00:24:02,745
I got to do homework.
Okay.

532
00:24:02,919 --> 00:24:04,225
Love you.
I love you.

533
00:24:04,399 --> 00:24:06,401
Happy birthday.
Thank you.

534
00:24:06,575 --> 00:24:08,490
Okay, I’m taking this.

535
00:24:10,405 --> 00:24:12,276
Good night!
Good night.

536
00:24:18,544 --> 00:24:19,545
(clatters)

537
00:24:24,201 --> 00:24:25,899
(whirring)

538
00:24:30,947 --> 00:24:33,167
Um, no eggs and bacon?

539
00:24:33,341 --> 00:24:35,604
I’m sorry. Did you predict
that I would have

540
00:24:35,778 --> 00:24:37,650
made you breakfast
this morning?

541
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,218
You’re hungry. Um...

542
00:24:41,392 --> 00:24:43,220
Yeah.
Okay.

543
00:24:43,394 --> 00:24:44,787
(Jenny) Knock knock!
Hi.

544
00:24:44,961 --> 00:24:46,006
Knock...

545
00:24:46,180 --> 00:24:48,095
(Morgan) Good catch. Hello.
Hello!

546
00:24:48,269 --> 00:24:50,401
My date for the day!

547
00:24:50,576 --> 00:24:53,187
So, I wrote down his feeding
schedule and sleep schedule.

548
00:24:53,361 --> 00:24:54,971
And he has this bad--

549
00:24:55,145 --> 00:24:58,409
Jenny... you do realize
I’ve raised a human, right?

550
00:24:58,584 --> 00:24:59,672
Two if we count you?

551
00:25:00,542 --> 00:25:01,543
<i>Touché.</i>

552
00:25:03,763 --> 00:25:05,460
Oh. Thanks, honey.
You’re welcome.

553
00:25:05,634 --> 00:25:07,723
Count me out
for dinner tonight. I have a staff meeting.

554
00:25:07,897 --> 00:25:09,116
Okay.

555
00:25:09,290 --> 00:25:11,597
Clara, honey.
Your car is blocking me in.

556
00:25:13,903 --> 00:25:15,644
Hello. Earth to Clara.

557
00:25:17,298 --> 00:25:19,561
(Chris) Car?
Right. Uh-huh...

558
00:25:19,735 --> 00:25:20,780
Bye!
(Morgan) Bye.

559
00:25:20,954 --> 00:25:21,781
(Chris) Bye.
I love you.

560
00:25:21,955 --> 00:25:22,912
(Chris and Clara) Love you!

561
00:25:23,086 --> 00:25:24,131
Okay, man.

562
00:25:26,437 --> 00:25:29,440
There you go.
Yes, oh, yes.

563
00:25:29,615 --> 00:25:31,268
What do you say you skip work,

564
00:25:31,442 --> 00:25:33,923
I skip school,
we go and see a double feature?

565
00:25:34,097 --> 00:25:36,752
I wish. Rain check?

566
00:25:36,926 --> 00:25:38,449
Lame.
Hey...

567
00:25:39,146 --> 00:25:40,495
you okay?

568
00:25:40,669 --> 00:25:43,933
Yeah, just... you know,
school drama. (sighs)

569
00:25:44,107 --> 00:25:45,413
Come here.
Hmm.

570
00:25:45,587 --> 00:25:46,806
You know I’m always here
if you need me.

571
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:49,678
Yeah. Love you.
Okay? I love you.

572
00:25:49,852 --> 00:25:50,810
I’ll see you tonight.

573
00:25:50,984 --> 00:25:52,681
Sure.Okay.

574
00:25:52,855 --> 00:25:53,856
Hey.

575
00:25:55,031 --> 00:25:57,599
What?
Miller unfollowed me.

576
00:25:57,773 --> 00:26:00,297
Uh, why?
Did you guys get in a fight?

577
00:26:00,471 --> 00:26:02,822
No! We haven’t even spoken
since I dropped him off.

578
00:26:02,996 --> 00:26:04,911
Clara. Honey. I’m blocked in.

579
00:26:05,085 --> 00:26:07,391
Uh, God,
I’m looking for my keys.

580
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,784
Why would he follow me

581
00:26:08,958 --> 00:26:10,569
just to unfollow me
a couple hours later?

582
00:26:10,743 --> 00:26:13,267
I mean...
social media is... confusing?

583
00:26:13,441 --> 00:26:14,442
I don’t know.

584
00:26:14,616 --> 00:26:16,270
Yeah, so are guys.

585
00:26:16,444 --> 00:26:17,619
(car honks)

586
00:26:17,793 --> 00:26:18,925
(Clara chuckles)

587
00:26:19,099 --> 00:26:20,753
(scoffs)

588
00:26:20,927 --> 00:26:22,842
(chuckles)
I love you, Clare Bear.

589
00:26:23,016 --> 00:26:24,670
Mmm, love you.

590
00:26:24,844 --> 00:26:26,236
Mmm... (mumbles)
(both grunting softly)

591
00:26:29,849 --> 00:26:30,763
Bye.

592
00:26:30,937 --> 00:26:31,894
Have fun.

593
00:26:33,026 --> 00:26:35,855
First day back! Whoo!
(chuckles)

594
00:26:36,682 --> 00:26:39,859
("My Fun" playing)

595
00:26:41,382 --> 00:26:42,513
(car honks)

596
00:26:43,950 --> 00:26:46,082
Hey, bitch! (chuckles)
(Clara) Hi.

597
00:26:46,256 --> 00:26:47,780
(Clara grunts)

598
00:26:47,954 --> 00:26:49,782
Thank you.
Mm-hmm. Milady.

599
00:26:49,956 --> 00:26:51,392
Oh, a gift.

600
00:26:51,566 --> 00:26:54,134
Oh, you shouldn’t have. Mm.I know.

601
00:26:54,308 --> 00:26:55,701
♪ <i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

602
00:26:55,875 --> 00:26:58,660
♪ <i>Yeah, babe</i>
<i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

603
00:26:58,834 --> 00:26:59,923
♪ <i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

604
00:26:59,947 --> 00:27:01,073
(Lexie and Clara
continue chattering indistinctly)

605
00:27:01,097 --> 00:27:03,273
♪ <i>Yeah, babe</i>
<i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

606
00:27:03,447 --> 00:27:05,841
♪ <i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

607
00:27:06,015 --> 00:27:08,409
♪ <i>Yeah, babe</i>
<i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

608
00:27:08,583 --> 00:27:10,933
♪ <i>You got a good woman</i>♪

609
00:27:11,107 --> 00:27:13,196
♪ <i>Yeah, babe</i>
<i>You got a good woman</i> ♪

610
00:27:13,370 --> 00:27:15,677
(song ends)

611
00:27:15,851 --> 00:27:17,026
(cell phone buzzes)

612
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,462
(distant chattering)

613
00:27:19,376 --> 00:27:21,030
Oh, shit!

614
00:27:21,204 --> 00:27:22,989
Miller and Shelby
broke up last night.

615
00:27:23,163 --> 00:27:24,251
(scoffs)

616
00:27:24,425 --> 00:27:26,209
Wait. Who told you that?
Emily.

617
00:27:26,383 --> 00:27:27,689
She called her, crying.

618
00:27:27,863 --> 00:27:31,084
Apparently they had a fight
because Miller...

619
00:27:31,258 --> 00:27:35,523
No, no, no. Shelby thought
Miller cheated on her with you.

620
00:27:35,697 --> 00:27:38,308
(laughing) Are you serious?
(chuckles) Yeah. Oh, my God.

621
00:27:38,482 --> 00:27:40,484
Well, I just gave him
a ride home.

622
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:41,964
Uh-huh. Right.

623
00:27:42,138 --> 00:27:44,532
There are all different
types of rides, Clara.

624
00:27:44,706 --> 00:27:46,882
Ew! Stop it!

625
00:27:47,056 --> 00:27:49,058
(indistinct chattering)

626
00:27:51,844 --> 00:27:52,758
(Lexie) Hey, Uncle Teach.

627
00:27:52,932 --> 00:27:54,934
Good morning.
(Jonah) Hey.

628
00:27:57,937 --> 00:28:00,853
Hey, Mr. Sullivan.
You wanted to talk to me?

629
00:28:01,027 --> 00:28:04,944
Yeah, um... I, uh,
thought you might want to know about this.

630
00:28:09,122 --> 00:28:11,080
It’ll look great for the film
schools you’re applying to.

631
00:28:13,517 --> 00:28:17,652
Lots of talented students
in the drama club could help you out.

632
00:28:17,826 --> 00:28:20,829
Yeah, no, thanks. I just don’t think
film school’s in the cards for me.

633
00:28:21,003 --> 00:28:23,484
You never know.
Keep it, just in case.

634
00:28:25,573 --> 00:28:26,617
Yeah.

635
00:28:32,754 --> 00:28:34,669
(school bell ringing)

636
00:28:34,843 --> 00:28:35,975
(indistinct chatter)

637
00:28:40,544 --> 00:28:41,763
(Clara) <i>You busy?</i>

638
00:28:43,112 --> 00:28:44,766
(Jenny) <i>On my way to lunch.</i>
<i>What’s up?</i>

639
00:28:46,289 --> 00:28:48,552
(Clara) <i>Miller and</i>
<i>his girlfriend broke up.</i>

640
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:50,163
(Jenny) <i>That’s great!</i>

641
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:56,082
(Clara) <i>I’m pretty sure he’s </i>
<i>trying to get her back. So...</i>

642
00:28:56,256 --> 00:28:59,999
(Jenny) <i>You don’t want to be</i>
<i>the other girl. Trust me!</i>

643
00:29:00,173 --> 00:29:02,915
(Clara) <i>Wait, you were</i>
<i>the other girl once?</i>

644
00:29:07,658 --> 00:29:09,704
<i>I need to hear about this!</i>

645
00:29:09,878 --> 00:29:12,054
<i>Come on,</i>
<i>I tell you everything.</i>

646
00:29:12,794 --> 00:29:13,839
<i>Hello?</i>

647
00:29:15,884 --> 00:29:17,016
(boy) Watch out!

648
00:29:17,190 --> 00:29:18,887
(all exclaim)
What the--? Oh, my God!

649
00:29:19,061 --> 00:29:22,021
Who threw that? Who threw that?
Who threw that?

650
00:29:22,195 --> 00:29:24,284
You got some
teeth coming, buddy?

651
00:29:25,067 --> 00:29:26,112
Yeah?

652
00:29:26,286 --> 00:29:28,070
That must hurt so much.

653
00:29:28,244 --> 00:29:30,769
(cell phone buzzing)
Oh. My phone’s ringing.

654
00:29:32,118 --> 00:29:34,163
(cell phone buzzing)

655
00:29:36,513 --> 00:29:37,558
Hello.

656
00:29:38,385 --> 00:29:40,082
Yes, this is she.

657
00:29:42,955 --> 00:29:44,086
What?

658
00:29:44,260 --> 00:29:45,827
(telephone ringing)

659
00:29:46,001 --> 00:29:47,046
Excuse me?

660
00:29:47,220 --> 00:29:48,787
Hi, my name is Morgan Grant.

661
00:29:48,961 --> 00:29:51,398
Um, my husband,
Chris Grant, works here.

662
00:29:51,572 --> 00:29:53,008
They said he was
in a car accident.

663
00:29:53,182 --> 00:29:54,357
(attendant)
Okay. Just have a seat

664
00:29:54,531 --> 00:29:55,663
and I’ll call the doctor
for you.

665
00:29:55,837 --> 00:29:57,491
Is he okay?
Can I talk to him?

666
00:29:57,665 --> 00:29:59,275
(attendant) Let me
get someone to help you. Okay?

667
00:29:59,449 --> 00:30:01,277
(sighs) Okay, could you
try paging my sister?

668
00:30:01,451 --> 00:30:02,583
She works here
in labor and delivery.

669
00:30:02,757 --> 00:30:04,803
Her name is Jenny Davidson.Morgan.

670
00:30:04,977 --> 00:30:07,675
Is he okay? Is Chris okay?
(Jonah) Hi.

671
00:30:09,155 --> 00:30:10,721
Chris? What?

672
00:30:10,896 --> 00:30:12,593
I keep trying to call Jenny,
but she’s not picking up.

673
00:30:12,767 --> 00:30:14,551
Wait,
why are you calling Jenny?

674
00:30:14,725 --> 00:30:16,553
What are you talking about?
Chris was in a car accident.

675
00:30:16,727 --> 00:30:19,034
They told me Jenny
was in a car accident.

676
00:30:25,998 --> 00:30:27,913
Can we get some help?
(woman) I’m working on it.

677
00:30:28,087 --> 00:30:30,089
Please!(Jonah slams desk)

678
00:30:38,749 --> 00:30:39,750
I’m very sorry.

679
00:30:39,925 --> 00:30:41,840
(somber music playing)

680
00:31:23,620 --> 00:31:25,666
(sobbing)

681
00:31:47,035 --> 00:31:48,645
Yeah. Okay.

682
00:31:48,819 --> 00:31:50,604
Yeah, thank you, Officer.

683
00:31:56,523 --> 00:31:58,786
(sighs) It was Jenny’s car.
Chris was driving.

684
00:32:00,483 --> 00:32:03,225
Her boss said she wasn’t due
back to work until tomorrow.

685
00:32:03,399 --> 00:32:05,793
That she was still
on maternity leave.

686
00:32:08,056 --> 00:32:09,188
Jesus,

687
00:32:09,362 --> 00:32:10,667
were they having an affair?Don’t.

688
00:32:10,841 --> 00:32:12,017
I-- What else could it be?

689
00:32:12,191 --> 00:32:13,192
No!

690
00:32:16,064 --> 00:32:17,413
I have two funerals to plan.

691
00:32:17,587 --> 00:32:19,589
(tender music playing)

692
00:32:29,164 --> 00:32:32,994
(pastor) "We were buried
with Him by baptism into death.

693
00:32:33,168 --> 00:32:34,865
So that as Christ
was raised from the dead

694
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:36,345
by the glory of the Father,

695
00:32:36,519 --> 00:32:40,349
we too might walk
into the newness of life."

696
00:32:42,177 --> 00:32:44,005
It is in that new life

697
00:32:44,179 --> 00:32:46,616
that Romans speaks of
that I wish...

698
00:32:46,790 --> 00:32:48,053
I need air.

699
00:32:48,227 --> 00:32:49,837
(pastor) ...for all
who grieve here today.

700
00:32:56,365 --> 00:32:58,063
(sobs softly)

701
00:33:00,848 --> 00:33:02,893
(continues sobbing)

702
00:33:37,885 --> 00:33:40,496
I met Chris
when we were in high school.

703
00:33:43,151 --> 00:33:46,067
Everyone wanted
to be his friend.

704
00:33:47,286 --> 00:33:49,288
His magnetism was...

705
00:33:52,204 --> 00:33:53,466
undeniable.

706
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:55,642
(footsteps approach)

707
00:34:06,914 --> 00:34:07,958
Hi.

708
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:19,622
I just couldn’t take it.

709
00:34:21,494 --> 00:34:22,495
It’s...

710
00:34:23,713 --> 00:34:25,106
unbearable.

711
00:34:27,630 --> 00:34:29,415
It’s like she separated
Dad and Aunt Jenny’s funeral

712
00:34:29,589 --> 00:34:31,547
just to torture us all.

713
00:34:36,422 --> 00:34:38,946
(inhales)
I just want to leave. (sighs)

714
00:34:43,342 --> 00:34:44,865
Then let’s leave.

715
00:34:45,996 --> 00:34:48,086
("Mountain" playing)

716
00:34:48,260 --> 00:34:52,177
♪ <i>Losing you is a mountain</i> ♪

717
00:34:54,222 --> 00:34:56,485
♪ <i>Of stillness</i> ♪

718
00:35:02,361 --> 00:35:04,537
(song continues playing)

719
00:35:06,278 --> 00:35:08,193
I feel like getting high.

720
00:35:09,629 --> 00:35:11,239
I’m sure you do.

721
00:35:13,285 --> 00:35:15,113
I’ve never tried it, and I...

722
00:35:15,287 --> 00:35:17,854
really feel like getting
out of my head right now.

723
00:35:19,465 --> 00:35:20,640
Do you have any?

724
00:35:21,771 --> 00:35:23,512
Uh, no. No, I don’t smoke.

725
00:35:25,471 --> 00:35:27,168
But I know how to get some.

726
00:35:29,431 --> 00:35:31,694
Yeah, right. You don’t smoke,
you just have a dealer?

727
00:35:31,868 --> 00:35:33,479
(chuckles)
No, she’s not a dealer.

728
00:35:33,653 --> 00:35:35,394
She’s just my stoner friend.

729
00:35:35,568 --> 00:35:36,960
Hmm.

730
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:39,746
♪ <i>Play it on over</i>
<i>And over again</i> ♪

731
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:41,356
Thanks.

732
00:35:41,530 --> 00:35:44,490
♪ <i>Play it on over</i>
<i>And over again</i> ♪

733
00:35:44,664 --> 00:35:48,537
♪ <i>Play it on over</i>
<i>And over again</i> ♪

734
00:35:48,711 --> 00:35:52,976
♪ <i>Play it on over</i>
<i>And over again</i> ♪

735
00:35:54,587 --> 00:35:56,415
(song ends)
Okay.

736
00:35:58,765 --> 00:36:00,070
Your weed, madam.

737
00:36:02,769 --> 00:36:03,944
Can you light it for me?

738
00:36:04,118 --> 00:36:05,424
Yeah.

739
00:36:05,598 --> 00:36:07,165
I’ve never even smoked
a cigarette before.

740
00:36:07,339 --> 00:36:10,907
(chuckles)
Good. You’ll live longer. Okay, ready?

741
00:36:11,081 --> 00:36:12,170
Yeah.

742
00:36:15,651 --> 00:36:16,913
(coughing)

743
00:36:18,350 --> 00:36:19,916
You okay?
Oh, my God!

744
00:36:20,090 --> 00:36:21,135
Yeah.

745
00:36:24,269 --> 00:36:25,705
Don’t look at me.
(continues coughing)

746
00:36:25,879 --> 00:36:27,881
(laughs)

747
00:36:28,055 --> 00:36:29,404
(chuckling) It’s terrible!

748
00:36:30,449 --> 00:36:32,538
Yeah. Yeah.

749
00:36:32,712 --> 00:36:34,714
I’m so sorry.
Thank you for being here.

750
00:36:36,846 --> 00:36:38,108
Hi.
Hi.

751
00:36:39,109 --> 00:36:40,807
(sighs) I’m so sorry.

752
00:36:40,981 --> 00:36:42,374
Um, where is Clara?

753
00:36:42,548 --> 00:36:45,290
Oh. I thought
she was with you.

754
00:36:45,464 --> 00:36:46,769
No.

755
00:36:46,943 --> 00:36:49,337
I’m sorry. I don’t--
It’s okay.

756
00:36:58,868 --> 00:37:01,131
I’m not feeling anything.

757
00:37:03,743 --> 00:37:05,440
(laughs)

758
00:37:05,614 --> 00:37:07,442
You are so stoned.

759
00:37:07,616 --> 00:37:08,965
Stop it.
No, I’m kidding. You done?

760
00:37:09,139 --> 00:37:11,011
You’re freaking me out.

761
00:37:14,928 --> 00:37:17,104
I saw your photos on Instagram.

762
00:37:18,018 --> 00:37:19,585
Before the unfollow.

763
00:37:20,934 --> 00:37:22,109
You’re really good.

764
00:37:22,283 --> 00:37:24,720
Thanks. Appreciate it.

765
00:37:28,550 --> 00:37:31,814
You know, now that
you’re single, you can...

766
00:37:32,598 --> 00:37:34,382
always follow me again.

767
00:37:38,038 --> 00:37:40,345
Shelby and I
got back together.

768
00:37:44,131 --> 00:37:46,612
Do you think
I’m into you or something?

769
00:37:46,786 --> 00:37:49,789
Is that why you need to keep informing me
of your relationship status?

770
00:37:49,963 --> 00:37:52,182
Has anyone ever told you
you can be kind of abrasive?

771
00:37:52,357 --> 00:37:54,402
Not in a negative way, but...
No, don’t change the subject.

772
00:37:54,576 --> 00:37:55,969
I mean, if you’re back
with your girlfriend,

773
00:37:56,143 --> 00:37:57,710
why are you here?

774
00:37:57,884 --> 00:38:00,321
I would’ve felt worse
if I didn’t check on you.

775
00:38:02,367 --> 00:38:03,759
Clara Grant!

776
00:38:03,933 --> 00:38:06,153
Oh, my God. Shit!

777
00:38:06,327 --> 00:38:08,198
My mom tracks us all.

778
00:38:08,373 --> 00:38:09,852
Clara Wilma Grant!

779
00:38:10,026 --> 00:38:12,115
(chuckles)
"Wilma?" That can’t be good.

780
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:14,248
No, full name equals grounded.

781
00:38:14,422 --> 00:38:15,902
Get in the car.
I’ve been calling you!

782
00:38:16,076 --> 00:38:17,817
(thuds)

783
00:38:19,253 --> 00:38:20,559
One second.

784
00:38:29,742 --> 00:38:31,134
Please pretend
this isn’t happening.

785
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:32,397
Is this better?
Yes!

786
00:38:32,571 --> 00:38:34,486
Get in the car.

787
00:38:34,660 --> 00:38:35,661
Good luck.

788
00:38:41,536 --> 00:38:43,538
(door handle rattling)

789
00:38:47,107 --> 00:38:49,109
Stop staring at him.

790
00:38:52,504 --> 00:38:55,507
Do you have any idea
how worried I was?

791
00:38:55,681 --> 00:38:58,466
Why do we even pay for a phone
if you never answer it?

792
00:38:59,859 --> 00:39:01,991
Sorry.
Oh, great. Thanks for saying "sorry."

793
00:39:02,165 --> 00:39:03,428
Everything’s fine now.

794
00:39:03,602 --> 00:39:05,647
Was that who I think it was?

795
00:39:06,735 --> 00:39:08,258
Look at me! Now!

796
00:39:08,433 --> 00:39:09,912
(gasps)What?

797
00:39:10,086 --> 00:39:11,914
Oh... Were you
smoking pot with him?

798
00:39:12,088 --> 00:39:13,916
What? No!

799
00:39:14,090 --> 00:39:17,050
And his name is Miller,
and no, we were just talking.

800
00:39:17,224 --> 00:39:20,445
You skipped your father’s
funeral to get high?

801
00:39:20,619 --> 00:39:22,229
Well, I stayed for most of it.

802
00:39:22,403 --> 00:39:24,623
It was
your father’s funeral.

803
00:39:24,797 --> 00:39:27,974
Okay, and we should have
just had one funeral for the both of them!

804
00:39:32,065 --> 00:39:33,893
How long am I grounded for?

805
00:39:37,244 --> 00:39:38,506
Forever. Like...

806
00:40:10,712 --> 00:40:12,061
(exhales)

807
00:40:34,257 --> 00:40:35,302
(blows)

808
00:41:00,849 --> 00:41:02,764
<i>We should really</i>
<i>toast to burning in hell.</i>

809
00:41:02,938 --> 00:41:04,723
<i>Yeah! To...</i>
<i>Outer Darkness.</i>

810
00:41:04,897 --> 00:41:06,768
<i>To Outer Darkness!</i>

811
00:41:06,942 --> 00:41:08,727
<i>Outer Darkness is </i>
<i>the lowest degree of heaven...</i>

812
00:41:08,901 --> 00:41:10,511
(knock on door)
<i>...in the Mormon faith.</i>

813
00:41:10,685 --> 00:41:12,861
<i>You have the Celestial Degree, </i>
<i>which is--</i>

814
00:41:13,035 --> 00:41:14,297
(knock on door)

815
00:41:19,085 --> 00:41:20,129
Hello.Hey.

816
00:41:20,303 --> 00:41:21,348
Come in.

817
00:41:22,871 --> 00:41:23,872
Okay.

818
00:41:31,750 --> 00:41:33,882
I, uh... I tried calling.

819
00:41:34,056 --> 00:41:36,015
Just wanted to make sure
you were okay.

820
00:41:36,189 --> 00:41:38,234
Aw, that’s nice of you.

821
00:41:40,541 --> 00:41:42,761
(sighs) I’m so good.

822
00:41:44,980 --> 00:41:46,025
Where’s Elijah?

823
00:41:46,199 --> 00:41:47,809
Uh, my mom’s got him.

824
00:41:49,724 --> 00:41:51,596
You’re sleeping
on the couch?

825
00:41:52,248 --> 00:41:53,511
Yes, I am.

826
00:41:55,121 --> 00:41:57,515
I’m also drinking wine.
Would you like to join me?

827
00:41:57,689 --> 00:41:59,212
I’m okay.

828
00:42:03,433 --> 00:42:05,305
Look, we need to talk.
Mmm...

829
00:42:06,219 --> 00:42:07,394
Nah, I’m good.

830
00:42:07,568 --> 00:42:09,439
Don’t you want to know
why they lied?

831
00:42:09,614 --> 00:42:11,703
No.
Why they were together?

832
00:42:11,877 --> 00:42:13,226
Why Chris
was driving her car?

833
00:42:13,400 --> 00:42:15,489
Jonah... (shushes)

834
00:42:15,663 --> 00:42:16,882
(softly)
Clara could hear you.

835
00:42:17,056 --> 00:42:19,537
And where is Chris’s car,
by the way?

836
00:42:31,070 --> 00:42:33,420
(breath shudders)

837
00:42:35,248 --> 00:42:37,119
Do you want that drink now?

838
00:42:40,732 --> 00:42:41,733
(sighs)

839
00:42:42,777 --> 00:42:44,387
(car doors opening and closing)

840
00:42:45,954 --> 00:42:48,566
(engine starts)
(sighs)

841
00:42:49,436 --> 00:42:51,264
(car departing)

842
00:43:14,461 --> 00:43:16,289
(Morgan) Oh, my God.
There’s his car.

843
00:43:30,564 --> 00:43:32,348
You stay here, I’ll go.

844
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:48,103
Popcorn still hot?

845
00:43:48,277 --> 00:43:49,757
Clara?

846
00:43:49,931 --> 00:43:52,586
(scoffs) I thought for sure
you’d be grounded.

847
00:43:52,760 --> 00:43:55,415
Yeah. No, I am. But I escaped.
(shushes)

848
00:43:55,589 --> 00:43:59,114
(chuckles) Theater 4 has
about 30 minutes left. Um...

849
00:43:59,288 --> 00:44:00,681
What’s playing?

850
00:44:00,855 --> 00:44:02,030
Oh, the latest
<i>Mission: Impossible.</i> You know...

851
00:44:02,204 --> 00:44:05,120
Tom Cruise saves the world
by running fast.

852
00:44:06,644 --> 00:44:07,557
(chuckles) Great.

853
00:44:07,732 --> 00:44:09,603
Perfect, I’ll take it.

854
00:44:10,909 --> 00:44:12,084
No, no, family gets in free.

855
00:44:12,258 --> 00:44:14,042
So if anyone asks,
you’re my sister.

856
00:44:16,566 --> 00:44:18,525
Right. (chuckles)

857
00:44:18,699 --> 00:44:21,180
Um, I think I’d almost
rather pay than pretend we’re siblings.

858
00:44:21,354 --> 00:44:22,616
(chuckles)

859
00:44:24,096 --> 00:44:25,445
Uh, you got, um...

860
00:44:39,764 --> 00:44:40,852
Theater 4.

861
00:44:43,202 --> 00:44:45,204
Right. Thanks.

862
00:44:47,119 --> 00:44:48,120
(sighs)

863
00:44:50,383 --> 00:44:51,776
Don’t start.

864
00:44:55,736 --> 00:44:57,172
(car door opens)

865
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:02,961
(sighs)

866
00:45:03,135 --> 00:45:04,876
He used to bring me here.

867
00:45:07,139 --> 00:45:08,967
On getaways.

868
00:45:09,141 --> 00:45:10,708
I’m sorry.

869
00:45:14,015 --> 00:45:17,062
They never checked out
and left all their shit.

870
00:45:19,281 --> 00:45:20,892
(sighs)

871
00:45:21,066 --> 00:45:23,416
I gave this to Jenny
last Christmas.

872
00:45:25,548 --> 00:45:26,593
Morgan, wait.

873
00:45:40,912 --> 00:45:43,784
Wait, where are you going?
Morgan!

874
00:45:43,958 --> 00:45:46,178
(Morgan) Asshole.
(Jonah) Oh, shit.

875
00:45:47,614 --> 00:45:48,571
Oh, shit. Morgan.

876
00:45:48,746 --> 00:45:50,748
(grunting loudly)
(thudding)

877
00:45:52,619 --> 00:45:55,753
(screaming)
I did everything for them!

878
00:45:59,582 --> 00:46:01,628
(car alarm blaring)
(grunting)

879
00:46:08,287 --> 00:46:09,418
Fuck!

880
00:46:09,592 --> 00:46:11,725
(continues grunting loudly)

881
00:46:14,249 --> 00:46:15,685
(screams)

882
00:46:21,213 --> 00:46:23,476
Didn’t know this movie
was a tearjerker.

883
00:46:23,650 --> 00:46:25,565
Yeah, uh...

884
00:46:25,739 --> 00:46:27,654
my dad loved movies.

885
00:46:29,134 --> 00:46:31,179
We used to come here a lot.

886
00:46:32,267 --> 00:46:33,703
That’s why I was crying.

887
00:46:34,487 --> 00:46:36,184
You know, um...

888
00:46:36,358 --> 00:46:38,665
Refuge Coffee plays, like,
old horror movies once a month.

889
00:46:38,839 --> 00:46:40,928
So, you know, if you want to...

890
00:46:44,410 --> 00:46:45,933
I should probably get going.

891
00:46:49,415 --> 00:46:51,330
I’m sorry,
did I say something wrong?

892
00:46:51,504 --> 00:46:53,636
No, um, just...

893
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:55,900
smiling feels wrong right now.
(sniffles)

894
00:46:56,074 --> 00:46:58,076
But I’ll see you at school.

895
00:46:58,250 --> 00:46:59,251
Yeah.

896
00:47:03,777 --> 00:47:04,996
Thank you.

897
00:47:08,086 --> 00:47:09,304
How are you so calm?

898
00:47:10,305 --> 00:47:12,612
Trust me, I’m not, but...

899
00:47:14,222 --> 00:47:16,746
I don’t know...
they cut you deeper than me.

900
00:47:19,227 --> 00:47:20,750
Clara can never know.

901
00:47:22,187 --> 00:47:25,843
She’s been
through enough already. Just promise me.

902
00:47:27,061 --> 00:47:29,020
She worshipped them.

903
00:47:30,151 --> 00:47:33,154
It would absolutely
destroy her.

904
00:47:35,200 --> 00:47:36,505
Yeah, okay.

905
00:47:48,387 --> 00:47:50,389
(engine starts)

906
00:47:51,346 --> 00:47:53,131
(sighs)

907
00:48:15,980 --> 00:48:18,330
(thuds)
Argh! Goddamn it!

908
00:48:19,722 --> 00:48:21,072
(grunts)
(crunches)

909
00:48:22,290 --> 00:48:24,031
Ugh! (strains)

910
00:48:27,817 --> 00:48:29,819
(Clara) What the hell?
(Morgan) Damn it!

911
00:48:31,734 --> 00:48:34,259
Mom? Oh, my God.
Mom, are you okay?

912
00:48:34,433 --> 00:48:37,175
What part of "grounded"
did you not understand?

913
00:48:37,349 --> 00:48:40,918
I’m sorry. You just left,
and I didn’t want to be alone.

914
00:48:41,092 --> 00:48:42,441
(sighs) Come on.

915
00:48:42,615 --> 00:48:44,182
What is happening? Dad’s car?

916
00:48:44,356 --> 00:48:47,054
I am tired, Clara.
I don’t want to talk about this.

917
00:48:47,228 --> 00:48:48,969
Who would do that?
Did you call the cops?

918
00:48:49,143 --> 00:48:50,362
It’s trashed!
You are grounded!

919
00:48:50,536 --> 00:48:52,364
Just go to your room!
Be in your room!

920
00:48:52,538 --> 00:48:54,061
What, I’m grounded
from the kitchen now?

921
00:48:54,235 --> 00:48:55,149
Yes!

922
00:48:58,805 --> 00:49:01,242
Ugh! (grunts)

923
00:49:01,416 --> 00:49:03,114
(panting)

924
00:49:29,879 --> 00:49:33,057
(Miller) <i>You get home okay?</i>
<i>Just checking on you.</i>

925
00:49:37,975 --> 00:49:40,107
(Clara) <i>Thanks for </i>
<i>cheering me up tonight.</i>

926
00:49:40,281 --> 00:49:42,892
<i>You’re the best sibling </i>
<i>I never had.</i>

927
00:49:43,067 --> 00:49:44,807
(knocking on door)

928
00:49:48,855 --> 00:49:50,117
(loud knocking on door)

929
00:49:50,291 --> 00:49:51,510
Jesus.

930
00:49:56,428 --> 00:49:58,343
Jonah, what’s going on?
It’s the middle of the night.

931
00:49:58,517 --> 00:49:59,866
I can’t do this.

932
00:50:00,040 --> 00:50:01,389
(Morgan) Is he okay?
He’s fine, I’m not.

933
00:50:01,563 --> 00:50:03,826
Hey, what’s going on?What?

934
00:50:04,001 --> 00:50:05,089
Hi, bubba.

935
00:50:05,263 --> 00:50:06,481
Do you mind
taking him for a second?

936
00:50:06,655 --> 00:50:08,005
I’m just gonna
talk to Jonah. Yeah.

937
00:50:08,179 --> 00:50:11,008
Hi, silly!
And here, take this. Jonah!

938
00:50:13,271 --> 00:50:15,838
What the hell
is going on with you?

939
00:50:17,492 --> 00:50:19,712
When he smiled tonight...
What? What happened?

940
00:50:19,886 --> 00:50:22,019
He has Chris’s fucking smile.

941
00:50:23,411 --> 00:50:24,499
(Clara) Everything okay?

942
00:50:24,673 --> 00:50:26,545
(car door opening and closing)

943
00:50:26,719 --> 00:50:27,850
Uh, yes! Yes, honey!

944
00:50:28,025 --> 00:50:30,331
Um, Jonah’s
just not feeling well.

945
00:50:30,505 --> 00:50:32,377
But do you mind feeding Elijah?
I think he’s hungry.

946
00:50:32,551 --> 00:50:34,466
Check if there’s
a bottle in the bag.

947
00:50:34,640 --> 00:50:35,684
Sure.

948
00:50:35,858 --> 00:50:37,077
Thank you.

949
00:50:37,251 --> 00:50:38,992
So what is your plan?

950
00:50:39,166 --> 00:50:40,820
I don’t know.
I need to clear my head.

951
00:50:40,994 --> 00:50:42,561
Oh, okay. Uh, when
will you be back?

952
00:50:42,735 --> 00:50:44,693
I don’t know.

953
00:50:44,867 --> 00:50:48,045
Okay, I see.
So you’re leaving again.

954
00:50:48,219 --> 00:50:49,959
You’re just gonna
dump your son on me

955
00:50:50,134 --> 00:50:53,137
and then you’re just gonna
come back who knows when?

956
00:50:53,311 --> 00:50:54,616
Not my son.

957
00:50:56,618 --> 00:51:00,622
("How’s It Going to Be"
playing)

958
00:51:07,673 --> 00:51:09,501
♪ <i>I’m only pretty sure</i> ♪

959
00:51:09,675 --> 00:51:13,026
♪ <i>That I can’t take any more</i> ♪

960
00:51:13,200 --> 00:51:16,334
♪ <i>Before you take a swing</i> ♪

961
00:51:16,508 --> 00:51:20,773
♪ <i>I wonder </i>
<i>What are we fighting for?</i> ♪

962
00:51:20,947 --> 00:51:26,170
♪ <i>When I say out loud </i>
<i>"I wanna get out of this"</i> ♪

963
00:51:26,344 --> 00:51:31,349
♪ <i>I wonder, is there anything </i>
<i>I’m gonna miss?</i> ♪

964
00:51:32,350 --> 00:51:33,655
(Morgan) Don’t judge me.

965
00:51:33,829 --> 00:51:37,224
<i>Receipts! Proof! Time line!</i>

966
00:51:37,398 --> 00:51:38,356
<i>Screenshots!</i>

967
00:51:38,530 --> 00:51:40,271
(bleep) <i>...everything to prove</i>

968
00:51:40,445 --> 00:51:44,362
<i>that you are a</i>(bleep) <i>bully </i>
<i>and a</i><i>(bleep) </i><i>troll...</i>

969
00:51:44,536 --> 00:51:46,146
(song fades)
Oh, hey, honey.

970
00:51:46,320 --> 00:51:48,061
(indistinct chattering over TV)

971
00:51:48,235 --> 00:51:49,236
Hmm...

972
00:51:50,063 --> 00:51:51,195
Okay.

973
00:51:53,458 --> 00:51:55,938
You’ve been in the same
clothes for days.

974
00:51:57,679 --> 00:51:58,724
Mm-hmm...

975
00:51:58,898 --> 00:52:01,901
You are camped out
on the couch.

976
00:52:02,075 --> 00:52:03,337
Oh, sorry.

977
00:52:03,511 --> 00:52:05,818
And you’re drinking,
which you never do.

978
00:52:05,992 --> 00:52:07,863
And you’re taking care
of somebody else’s kid?

979
00:52:08,037 --> 00:52:09,604
(Morgan) That reminds me.

980
00:52:09,778 --> 00:52:12,607
Can you go to the store
and pick up some formula?

981
00:52:12,781 --> 00:52:14,740
I went and I got everything
but formula,

982
00:52:14,914 --> 00:52:16,655
and we’ve just ran out.

983
00:52:16,829 --> 00:52:19,266
No, no, no. Tell Jonah to do it.
It’s his responsibility.

984
00:52:19,440 --> 00:52:22,661
Clara, his whole world
just got turned upside-down.

985
00:52:22,835 --> 00:52:24,967
Our world just got
turned upside-down.

986
00:52:25,881 --> 00:52:27,274
Well, I can’t go.

987
00:52:27,448 --> 00:52:30,408
Can you go?
Can you go? I love you.

988
00:52:30,582 --> 00:52:32,932
It’s the one
with the green label.

989
00:52:46,163 --> 00:52:48,991
(knocking on door)
(indistinct chattering over TV)

990
00:52:49,166 --> 00:52:51,429
Jonah, it’s been two days!

991
00:52:53,779 --> 00:52:56,782
Dude, I know you’re in there!
I can hear the TV.

992
00:52:57,739 --> 00:52:58,740
(doorbell ringing)

993
00:53:00,438 --> 00:53:01,961
(knocking on door continues)
Okay!

994
00:53:04,006 --> 00:53:05,051
Okay!

995
00:53:08,750 --> 00:53:09,795
(sighs)

996
00:53:10,535 --> 00:53:11,536
Geez.

997
00:53:13,059 --> 00:53:14,669
If the school board
ever saw this,

998
00:53:14,843 --> 00:53:16,802
you’d totally
be out of a job.

999
00:53:16,976 --> 00:53:18,543
Not that you care.

1000
00:53:19,892 --> 00:53:21,415
Dude, what are you doing?

1001
00:53:21,589 --> 00:53:22,721
Cleaning.

1002
00:53:22,895 --> 00:53:25,114
No, I mean
what are you doing?

1003
00:53:25,289 --> 00:53:27,378
Why is my mom
taking care of your kid?

1004
00:53:28,466 --> 00:53:30,642
(sighs)
You wouldn’t understand.

1005
00:53:31,860 --> 00:53:33,166
(chuckles) I love whenever

1006
00:53:33,340 --> 00:53:34,689
adults who are behaving
like children

1007
00:53:34,863 --> 00:53:36,343
say that to children
who are behaving like adults.

1008
00:53:36,517 --> 00:53:37,518
Clever.

1009
00:53:40,565 --> 00:53:42,610
Getting rid of Jenny’s stuff?

1010
00:53:42,784 --> 00:53:45,961
(sighs) She never really
got around to unpacking.

1011
00:53:46,135 --> 00:53:47,876
You know how she was.

1012
00:53:48,050 --> 00:53:49,269
Aren’t you even, like,

1013
00:53:49,443 --> 00:53:51,663
the tiniest bit worried
about Elijah?

1014
00:53:51,837 --> 00:53:53,578
Of course. I’m just...

1015
00:53:54,927 --> 00:53:56,885
I’m not in a good place, okay?

1016
00:53:57,059 --> 00:53:58,844
Yeah, and neither is my mom.

1017
00:53:59,018 --> 00:54:00,889
She just lost her husband
and her sister.

1018
00:54:01,063 --> 00:54:02,239
Yeah, and I just lost
my best friend

1019
00:54:02,413 --> 00:54:03,588
and the mother of my son.

1020
00:54:03,762 --> 00:54:06,417
And I just lost
my dad and my aunt.

1021
00:54:06,591 --> 00:54:08,549
Thanks. Now we’ve established
we’re all broken

1022
00:54:08,723 --> 00:54:10,377
and totally messed up.

1023
00:54:11,770 --> 00:54:12,684
You know what?

1024
00:54:12,858 --> 00:54:15,164
Elijah rolled over last night.

1025
00:54:16,688 --> 00:54:18,472
What, he did?

1026
00:54:18,646 --> 00:54:21,127
No, but he’s going to. Soon.

1027
00:54:21,301 --> 00:54:23,042
And you’re gonna miss it.

1028
00:54:23,216 --> 00:54:24,783
You’re gonna miss
all of these memories

1029
00:54:24,957 --> 00:54:26,393
that you’re
never gonna get back.

1030
00:54:28,656 --> 00:54:29,831
So...

1031
00:54:30,005 --> 00:54:32,007
how about you go
and get your son?

1032
00:54:34,445 --> 00:54:37,186
Hello? How about you go
and get your son? (sighs)

1033
00:54:39,276 --> 00:54:40,320
(softly) Yeah.

1034
00:54:43,323 --> 00:54:46,457
Um, also, I’ll clean your house
for 50 bucks.

1035
00:54:46,631 --> 00:54:48,502
Yeah, okay.
And...

1036
00:54:48,676 --> 00:54:50,939
on the way back,
get baby formula.

1037
00:54:51,113 --> 00:54:52,332
The one with the green label.

1038
00:54:52,506 --> 00:54:54,029
Got it. Thanks, Clara.

1039
00:54:58,556 --> 00:54:59,470
Hmm...

1040
00:54:59,644 --> 00:55:01,733
(babbles) Are you hungry?

1041
00:55:01,907 --> 00:55:03,430
Oh, perfect timing!

1042
00:55:03,604 --> 00:55:06,520
He is so hungry
and ready to eat.

1043
00:55:06,694 --> 00:55:08,000
Hey, can I?

1044
00:55:09,306 --> 00:55:11,177
(voice breaking)
I’m here, buddy. Daddy’s here.

1045
00:55:11,351 --> 00:55:12,700
(sobbing)

1046
00:55:12,874 --> 00:55:14,485
I’ll never leave you again.

1047
00:55:15,442 --> 00:55:17,183
How I love you.

1048
00:55:17,357 --> 00:55:18,576
(Elijah squeals)
I know, I know.

1049
00:55:18,750 --> 00:55:20,752
I’m mad at me, too, bud.

1050
00:55:24,799 --> 00:55:25,757
I’m sorry.

1051
00:55:26,497 --> 00:55:28,325
I’m so sorry.

1052
00:55:47,474 --> 00:55:48,475
(sniffles)

1053
00:55:57,484 --> 00:55:58,833
I’m so sorry.

1054
00:55:59,007 --> 00:56:00,835
(sobs softly)

1055
00:56:02,620 --> 00:56:03,621
(door closes)

1056
00:56:06,294 --> 00:56:07,194
Um, hi.

1057
00:56:07,219 --> 00:56:10,149
I sent you three minutes up the road
to get formula.

1058
00:56:10,323 --> 00:56:11,498
Where have you been?

1059
00:56:12,369 --> 00:56:13,370
Where’s Elijah?

1060
00:56:13,544 --> 00:56:14,675
Jonah came to pick him up.

1061
00:56:14,849 --> 00:56:15,981
What? That’s crazy.

1062
00:56:16,155 --> 00:56:17,983
Looks like
we don’t need formula.

1063
00:56:18,157 --> 00:56:21,508
Yeah, also crazy, you still
haven’t told me where you were.

1064
00:56:21,682 --> 00:56:25,164
Oh, my God. I am here now.
Why does it matter?

1065
00:56:25,338 --> 00:56:26,644
You were with Miller,
weren’t you?

1066
00:56:26,818 --> 00:56:29,211
Geez, Mom.
It’s like you always do this.

1067
00:56:29,386 --> 00:56:31,823
You have to control my life
because you don’t have one.

1068
00:56:31,997 --> 00:56:33,564
Can I go now?
No!

1069
00:56:33,738 --> 00:56:35,217
’Cause you still haven’t
told me where you were!

1070
00:56:35,392 --> 00:56:37,132
I was cleaning
Jonah’s house.

1071
00:56:37,306 --> 00:56:40,048
Yeah, right.
Solving your problems.

1072
00:56:40,222 --> 00:56:42,399
Why do you always
assume the worst of me?

1073
00:56:44,052 --> 00:56:45,140
(door closes)

1074
00:56:54,323 --> 00:56:55,629
(cell phone dings)

1075
00:56:55,803 --> 00:56:57,414
(Miller) <i>Where you at?</i>

1076
00:57:03,028 --> 00:57:04,290
(Clara) <i>Refuge.</i>

1077
00:57:05,900 --> 00:57:07,293
(Miller) <i>On my way.</i>

1078
00:57:14,213 --> 00:57:15,997
Stalk much?

1079
00:57:16,171 --> 00:57:18,347
It’s not my fault you’re not
aware of your surroundings.

1080
00:57:18,522 --> 00:57:20,045
Look.

1081
00:57:20,219 --> 00:57:21,873
I don’t know how I feel
about being your backup plan

1082
00:57:22,047 --> 00:57:23,614
every time things go south
with your girlfriend.

1083
00:57:23,788 --> 00:57:26,007
I don’t have a girlfriend.

1084
00:57:26,181 --> 00:57:28,096
I broke up with her.

1085
00:57:28,880 --> 00:57:29,794
For good.

1086
00:57:29,968 --> 00:57:31,970
You want to go for a ride?

1087
00:57:41,370 --> 00:57:43,677
Just smile and act natural.

1088
00:57:43,851 --> 00:57:46,419
(Clara) Why do I always
get roped into this?

1089
00:57:46,593 --> 00:57:48,595
The things we do for love.

1090
00:57:48,769 --> 00:57:50,858
Of... pizza.

1091
00:57:53,513 --> 00:57:54,514
(Clara chuckling)

1092
00:57:57,212 --> 00:57:58,475
He’s gonna take
your whole hand off.

1093
00:57:58,649 --> 00:57:59,650
I know.

1094
00:58:02,957 --> 00:58:04,002
How’s he doing?

1095
00:58:07,092 --> 00:58:08,136
Cancer.

1096
00:58:09,398 --> 00:58:11,139
I’m so sorry, Miller.

1097
00:58:12,097 --> 00:58:13,141
Yeah.

1098
00:58:17,145 --> 00:58:19,931
He’s kind of like
the only parent I ever had.

1099
00:58:20,105 --> 00:58:22,716
My mom died when I
was young and my dad...

1100
00:58:24,196 --> 00:58:25,240
Well, whatever.

1101
00:58:27,460 --> 00:58:29,984
Kind of makes it hard
to think about college.

1102
00:58:30,158 --> 00:58:32,857
You know, because I don’t know
who’s gonna look after him.

1103
00:58:35,294 --> 00:58:36,817
I think you are.

1104
00:58:36,991 --> 00:58:39,516
When we drive home together
on the weekends.

1105
00:58:41,822 --> 00:58:43,737
It’s like a two-hour drive.

1106
00:58:46,827 --> 00:58:49,221
Yeah, but I don’t even know
if I’m gonna get in, so...

1107
00:58:50,657 --> 00:58:52,529
Only one way to find out.

1108
00:58:58,491 --> 00:59:01,102
I should’ve gotten rid
of that door years ago.

1109
00:59:01,276 --> 00:59:02,539
Why didn’t you?

1110
00:59:02,713 --> 00:59:04,236
Well, it’s Chris’s
childhood home.

1111
00:59:04,410 --> 00:59:05,280
"Don’t change a thing."

1112
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:06,630
But...

1113
00:59:06,804 --> 00:59:09,502
here we are, 17 years later.

1114
00:59:11,765 --> 00:59:14,333
You know, I remember
in school seeing you draw rooms and houses

1115
00:59:14,507 --> 00:59:15,856
in the margins
of your papers.

1116
00:59:16,030 --> 00:59:17,118
You were really good.

1117
00:59:17,292 --> 00:59:18,511
You were spying on me?

1118
00:59:18,685 --> 00:59:20,295
(chuckles) I sat behind you.

1119
00:59:20,469 --> 00:59:21,949
Class was boring.
You weren’t.

1120
00:59:22,123 --> 00:59:24,299
Oh, you must be thinking
of someone else.

1121
00:59:24,473 --> 00:59:26,824
Trust me, I was never
thinking of anyone else.

1122
00:59:34,135 --> 00:59:36,311
(clears throat)
Clara should be home.

1123
00:59:39,837 --> 00:59:42,100
(sighs)
I am so late.

1124
00:59:46,452 --> 00:59:48,585
Okay, before you go,
I have to tell you something.

1125
00:59:50,499 --> 00:59:53,285
When you said
you were my backup plan, I wanted to laugh,

1126
00:59:53,459 --> 00:59:54,503
because...

1127
00:59:55,853 --> 00:59:59,117
if anything, Shelby
was my backup plan to you.

1128
01:00:00,118 --> 01:00:02,337
(scoffs)
What do you mean?

1129
01:00:02,511 --> 01:00:04,426
Look, the reason I broke up
with Shelby is because,

1130
01:00:04,601 --> 01:00:06,907
when I went to sleep at night,

1131
01:00:07,081 --> 01:00:09,518
I wasn’t thinking about her.

1132
01:00:09,693 --> 01:00:11,172
And when I woke up,
I wasn’t thinking

1133
01:00:11,346 --> 01:00:12,260
about her either, Clara.

1134
01:00:12,434 --> 01:00:14,045
I was thinking about you.

1135
01:00:15,655 --> 01:00:17,309
And I hated the way
that made me feel.

1136
01:00:17,483 --> 01:00:19,441
It made me feel like
I was cheating, or something.

1137
01:00:19,616 --> 01:00:21,618
And I’m not that kind of guy.

1138
01:00:27,536 --> 01:00:31,018
I’ve had a thing for you
for a very long time, too.

1139
01:00:33,673 --> 01:00:35,196
Okay, who’s the stalker now?

1140
01:00:41,072 --> 01:00:42,900
("Chesapeake" playing)

1141
01:00:43,074 --> 01:00:49,602
♪ <i>I can’t hardly wait</i> ♪

1142
01:00:49,776 --> 01:00:53,345
That’s not how I thought
our first kiss would be like.

1143
01:00:53,519 --> 01:00:55,477
(song continues playing)
Like what?

1144
01:00:56,522 --> 01:00:57,566
Sweet.

1145
01:00:59,046 --> 01:01:00,744
How did you think
it would be?

1146
01:01:02,833 --> 01:01:07,533
♪ <i>I was all covered in sound</i> ♪

1147
01:01:07,707 --> 01:01:09,187
Like this.

1148
01:01:09,361 --> 01:01:12,233
♪ <i>When you asked me</i>
<i>To turn it down</i> ♪

1149
01:01:12,407 --> 01:01:16,194
♪ <i>Didn’t even think</i>
<i>It was loud</i> ♪

1150
01:01:17,630 --> 01:01:24,593
♪ <i>Can you hear it now?</i> ♪

1151
01:01:29,947 --> 01:01:31,383
(cell phone buzzing)

1152
01:01:33,777 --> 01:01:35,996
<i>Hi, it’s Clara.</i>
<i>Leave a message.</i>

1153
01:01:36,170 --> 01:01:37,389
Nothing.
(phone line beeps)

1154
01:01:37,563 --> 01:01:38,956
Oh, she’s totally
screening my calls.

1155
01:01:41,741 --> 01:01:44,613
I should, uh... I should
probably go pick up Elijah.

1156
01:01:44,788 --> 01:01:46,050
How is he?

1157
01:01:46,964 --> 01:01:48,313
Good. Yeah.

1158
01:01:48,487 --> 01:01:51,490
My mom’s been a huge help.
Does she, um...

1159
01:01:52,709 --> 01:01:54,101
Does she know?

1160
01:01:55,407 --> 01:01:57,148
No, I didn’t tell her.

1161
01:01:59,498 --> 01:02:00,760
Look, I know you don’t think

1162
01:02:00,934 --> 01:02:02,370
it’s a good idea
to tell Clara, but...

1163
01:02:02,544 --> 01:02:04,416
if she and Elijah
are half-siblings...

1164
01:02:04,590 --> 01:02:07,375
Oh, my God.
Just hearing you say that is...

1165
01:02:07,549 --> 01:02:09,377
When he’s older,
he might want to know.

1166
01:02:09,551 --> 01:02:11,510
And I think she might, too.

1167
01:02:11,684 --> 01:02:13,338
Yeah, maybe. I don’t know.

1168
01:02:13,512 --> 01:02:16,907
I never know these days
what she wants.

1169
01:02:17,081 --> 01:02:20,171
I mean, she probably
doesn’t, either.

1170
01:02:21,085 --> 01:02:22,521
You remember that age.

1171
01:02:22,695 --> 01:02:26,525
Everything felt so intense,
complicated. (chuckles)

1172
01:02:27,308 --> 01:02:28,657
I...

1173
01:02:28,832 --> 01:02:31,399
I can’t really remember
what it felt like.

1174
01:02:32,923 --> 01:02:35,839
You know what gets me there
is the music of the time.

1175
01:02:37,057 --> 01:02:39,451
You hear a song
and it just wrecks you.

1176
01:02:39,625 --> 01:02:41,453
Takes you right back.

1177
01:02:42,584 --> 01:02:43,629
Okay...

1178
01:02:44,935 --> 01:02:46,110
try me.

1179
01:02:46,284 --> 01:02:47,894
(sighs)

1180
01:02:53,030 --> 01:02:55,032
("Dakota" playing
over cell phone)

1181
01:02:57,599 --> 01:02:59,036
What is this one again?

1182
01:02:59,993 --> 01:03:01,821
You really don’t remember?

1183
01:03:06,826 --> 01:03:09,960
("Dakota" continues playing
over speakers)

1184
01:03:14,312 --> 01:03:16,183
(gasps) Hey!

1185
01:03:16,357 --> 01:03:18,577
Hey, careful!

1186
01:03:18,751 --> 01:03:21,885
If you ruin this and I don’t
get into State, I am suing you.

1187
01:03:22,059 --> 01:03:24,583
It’s the weekend. Come swim!

1188
01:03:24,757 --> 01:03:26,628
(laughing) Come on.

1189
01:03:28,239 --> 01:03:29,544
I’m just gonna
keep splashing you

1190
01:03:29,718 --> 01:03:30,937
if you don’t come in.

1191
01:03:31,111 --> 01:03:32,765
No, you’re not.
All right. Here we go.

1192
01:03:32,939 --> 01:03:33,940
No!

1193
01:03:34,636 --> 01:03:35,681
(chuckles)

1194
01:03:36,900 --> 01:03:38,597
(Morgan) Okay.

1195
01:03:38,771 --> 01:03:41,339
That’s not bad.
It’s perfect.

1196
01:03:41,513 --> 01:03:42,688
(Morgan) Ooh...

1197
01:03:43,384 --> 01:03:45,082
Okay, are you satisfied?

1198
01:03:45,256 --> 01:03:46,692
Definitely. (chuckles)

1199
01:03:46,866 --> 01:03:48,128
Ooh.

1200
01:03:48,302 --> 01:03:50,217
♪ <i>Made me feel</i>
<i>Like the one</i> ♪

1201
01:03:50,391 --> 01:03:51,436
Ooh.

1202
01:03:52,480 --> 01:03:53,655
♪ <i>The one</i> ♪

1203
01:03:56,702 --> 01:04:00,053
♪ <i>You made me feel</i>
<i>Like the one</i> ♪

1204
01:04:00,227 --> 01:04:02,664
♪ <i>Made me feel</i>
<i>Like the one</i> ♪

1205
01:04:02,839 --> 01:04:04,841
I’m worried we got it wrong.

1206
01:04:05,624 --> 01:04:06,886
♪ <i>The one</i> ♪

1207
01:04:07,060 --> 01:04:09,149
(Jenny) Hey, look what
we got at the garage!

1208
01:04:09,323 --> 01:04:11,195
(Chris) Yo! What up?

1209
01:04:11,369 --> 01:04:15,460
That’s right.
Yeah, we have a party!

1210
01:04:15,634 --> 01:04:16,722
♪ <i>Drinking with you</i> ♪

1211
01:04:18,115 --> 01:04:20,030
♪ <i>When drinking was new</i> ♪

1212
01:04:20,204 --> 01:04:22,859
("Dakota" continues playing
over cell phone)

1213
01:04:24,817 --> 01:04:26,253
(Clara) Hey, I’m sorry.

1214
01:04:26,427 --> 01:04:27,733
I... I know that I’m late
and I’m grounded.

1215
01:04:28,865 --> 01:04:31,171
Um...
(song stops)

1216
01:04:31,345 --> 01:04:34,696
Um... My phone was off
and I was distracted. I’m...

1217
01:04:35,262 --> 01:04:36,263
sorry.

1218
01:04:40,441 --> 01:04:41,878
Hi.
(softly) Hey.

1219
01:04:45,359 --> 01:04:46,360
Yeah.

1220
01:04:47,709 --> 01:04:50,190
Yeah, yeah,
you’re very grounded.

1221
01:04:51,278 --> 01:04:53,541
Just go to your room, I guess.

1222
01:04:54,586 --> 01:04:56,631
That’s it?

1223
01:04:56,805 --> 01:04:59,330
(Morgan) Mmm...
No, it’s fine. Yeah. Okay.

1224
01:05:02,899 --> 01:05:06,424
I swear, I have no idea
what’s going on with my mom lately.

1225
01:05:09,906 --> 01:05:11,908
Yeah, give her time.
She’s dealing with a lot.

1226
01:05:16,695 --> 01:05:18,566
(Lexie) Whoa, hey!

1227
01:05:18,740 --> 01:05:20,829
Find a boyfriend for me yet?

1228
01:05:21,004 --> 01:05:23,223
Actually, yeah. Um...

1229
01:05:23,397 --> 01:05:25,356
You know Efren?
(Lexie) The AV nerd?

1230
01:05:25,530 --> 01:05:26,748
Yo, Efren!

1231
01:05:26,923 --> 01:05:28,359
(Efren) Ow! Oh...

1232
01:05:28,533 --> 01:05:29,838
Hey, hey, hey.

1233
01:05:30,013 --> 01:05:31,231
Oh...

1234
01:05:31,405 --> 01:05:33,407
Uh, come here, man.
(grunts)

1235
01:05:33,581 --> 01:05:35,148
(softly) Okay, hey.

1236
01:05:36,541 --> 01:05:37,803
He’s really nice.

1237
01:05:37,977 --> 01:05:39,239
(Lexie) Don’t tell him
to come over here.

1238
01:05:39,413 --> 01:05:41,154
No, you’ll love him.
What’s up, dude?

1239
01:05:41,328 --> 01:05:42,547
(sighs)

1240
01:05:42,721 --> 01:05:43,940
Hi, Efren.
(Efren) Hi, Clara.

1241
01:05:44,114 --> 01:05:45,550
What’s up, dude?
What’s up?

1242
01:05:46,464 --> 01:05:48,031
Do you know Lexie?

1243
01:05:48,205 --> 01:05:49,597
Uh, not really.

1244
01:05:49,771 --> 01:05:52,339
No. No offense, though!
It’s just that, um...

1245
01:05:53,471 --> 01:05:55,299
you always seemed
kind of scary.

1246
01:05:55,473 --> 01:05:56,735
I am scary.

1247
01:05:56,909 --> 01:05:58,606
Yeah, uh... (clears throat)

1248
01:05:58,780 --> 01:06:00,173
Do you have any tattoos?

1249
01:06:00,347 --> 01:06:02,436
(scoffing)
Hell, no! No! What?

1250
01:06:04,525 --> 01:06:06,266
Wait, why? Should I?

1251
01:06:06,440 --> 01:06:09,835
Don’t you have to be, like, 18?
(mumbles, chuckles awkwardly)

1252
01:06:10,009 --> 01:06:12,359
I don’t want
to do that, so, uh...

1253
01:06:16,450 --> 01:06:18,148
(knocking on door)

1254
01:06:22,152 --> 01:06:23,457
Hey.
Something’s wrong.

1255
01:06:23,631 --> 01:06:24,850
He feels really hot...
(Elijah fussing)

1256
01:06:25,024 --> 01:06:26,417
...and he’s not acting
like himself.

1257
01:06:26,591 --> 01:06:29,289
Okay, let’s see. Oh, bubba.

1258
01:06:29,463 --> 01:06:31,683
Oh, yeah, looks like
he’s got a little bug.

1259
01:06:31,857 --> 01:06:33,032
Feel the back of his neck.

1260
01:06:33,206 --> 01:06:34,991
Yeah. Buddy.Yeah.

1261
01:06:35,165 --> 01:06:37,036
Oh, we’re gonna take
care of you. Come here.

1262
01:06:37,210 --> 01:06:38,211
Okay.

1263
01:06:40,257 --> 01:06:43,129
Uh, acetaminophen
always helps.

1264
01:06:43,303 --> 01:06:45,392
It does.
But firsts are the worst.

1265
01:06:45,566 --> 01:06:47,873
First fall. First fever.
(Elijah fussing)

1266
01:06:48,047 --> 01:06:49,266
First tooth.

1267
01:06:49,440 --> 01:06:51,224
Oh. This is a cold.

1268
01:06:51,398 --> 01:06:52,921
God, how am I gonna
do this, buddy?

1269
01:06:53,096 --> 01:06:54,445
Oh, you just will.

1270
01:06:55,663 --> 01:06:57,317
Hey. Is Elijah all right?

1271
01:06:57,491 --> 01:06:59,189
Yeah, it’s just a cold.

1272
01:06:59,363 --> 01:07:01,191
Yeah, I’m still new at this.
Your mom’s helping me out.

1273
01:07:01,365 --> 01:07:02,279
Where are you going?

1274
01:07:02,453 --> 01:07:04,803
Um, to the movies with Lexie.

1275
01:07:04,804 --> 01:07:05,652
Oh, weird.

1276
01:07:05,677 --> 01:07:07,811
I didn’t realize Miller had
changed his name to Lexie.

1277
01:07:09,634 --> 01:07:10,983
Doesn’t he have
a girlfriend?

1278
01:07:11,157 --> 01:07:13,159
They broke up.
Oh, okay.

1279
01:07:13,333 --> 01:07:15,118
And 30 seconds later,
he’s with you.

1280
01:07:15,292 --> 01:07:17,468
Mom.
I’m just saying.

1281
01:07:17,642 --> 01:07:20,906
He’s not the kind of guy that’s worth
throwing your life away for, Clara.

1282
01:07:21,080 --> 01:07:23,343
(scoffing)
Throwing my life away?

1283
01:07:23,517 --> 01:07:25,693
Jesus, Mom,
I’m going to the movies.

1284
01:07:27,130 --> 01:07:29,045
(sighs)

1285
01:07:29,219 --> 01:07:31,960
Don’t look at me.
I’m Team Miller. (chuckles)

1286
01:07:32,135 --> 01:07:33,179
Sorry.

1287
01:07:33,353 --> 01:07:34,833
I am putting you
to work for that.

1288
01:07:35,007 --> 01:07:35,877
That’s fair.
Right?

1289
01:07:36,052 --> 01:07:37,444
Should we put Dada to work?

1290
01:07:38,489 --> 01:07:39,968
(Jonah) Ugh! Got it.

1291
01:07:41,405 --> 01:07:43,711
So, I think we can
just take this entire thing

1292
01:07:43,885 --> 01:07:44,973
down in one piece.

1293
01:07:45,148 --> 01:07:46,236
I just have to empty it.

1294
01:07:46,410 --> 01:07:48,716
(chair sliding)
I’m so excited!

1295
01:07:59,466 --> 01:08:00,685
(sighs)

1296
01:08:00,859 --> 01:08:01,903
Morgan.

1297
01:08:10,390 --> 01:08:11,696
This is Jenny’s handwriting.

1298
01:08:12,827 --> 01:08:15,178
Right under our noses?

1299
01:08:21,140 --> 01:08:23,534
I don’t need to read them.

1300
01:08:23,708 --> 01:08:26,450
Oh, come on. You’re not even
a little bit curious?

1301
01:08:26,624 --> 01:08:27,886
It’s in the past.

1302
01:08:28,060 --> 01:08:29,931
Huh... Must be nice.

1303
01:08:33,109 --> 01:08:36,764
You are not the one
living in his house.

1304
01:08:36,938 --> 01:08:38,679
Living in his parents’ house.

1305
01:08:38,853 --> 01:08:40,072
Surrounded by his things.

1306
01:08:40,246 --> 01:08:42,770
His stuff is everywhere!
It is everywhere!

1307
01:08:42,944 --> 01:08:44,946
That painting!
That horrible painting.

1308
01:08:45,121 --> 01:08:47,079
Jenny took me
to a specific place

1309
01:08:47,253 --> 01:08:48,646
to buy that painting
for Chris’s birthday,

1310
01:08:48,820 --> 01:08:51,866
and I was, like, "Chris?
A painting for his birthday?

1311
01:08:52,040 --> 01:08:53,564
Why are we doing this?"

1312
01:08:53,738 --> 01:08:55,522
And she was, like,
"You don’t know him like I do."

1313
01:08:55,696 --> 01:08:57,872
I thought she was kidding.

1314
01:08:58,046 --> 01:08:59,570
She wasn’t kidding.

1315
01:09:00,745 --> 01:09:02,921
All right. I have an idea.

1316
01:09:04,488 --> 01:09:05,924
Oh, my God,
I hate this thing.

1317
01:09:06,098 --> 01:09:07,317
I’m so excited. I’m doing this.
Go. Go. Go!

1318
01:09:07,491 --> 01:09:08,666
It’s gonna be messy.
Yes.

1319
01:09:08,840 --> 01:09:10,058
But it’s fine.
We don’t care.

1320
01:09:10,233 --> 01:09:11,495
Look at how ugly that thing is.
Ugh! Okay.

1321
01:09:11,669 --> 01:09:12,626
(groans)

1322
01:09:12,800 --> 01:09:14,062
Ugh! This painting!

1323
01:09:15,455 --> 01:09:17,631
Give it a little crow hop!
Oh, my God! (exclaims)

1324
01:09:17,805 --> 01:09:20,112
(grunting)

1325
01:09:22,070 --> 01:09:23,463
Don’t drag it.
Oh, there we go.

1326
01:09:23,637 --> 01:09:24,464
(Jonah grunts)

1327
01:09:24,638 --> 01:09:25,770
Okay.

1328
01:09:25,944 --> 01:09:27,032
(chuckles)
Where are we going?

1329
01:09:27,206 --> 01:09:28,729
Patience, Grasshopper.
Okay.

1330
01:09:28,903 --> 01:09:30,644
Okay.
Oh...

1331
01:09:32,168 --> 01:09:33,560
What is all this?

1332
01:09:33,734 --> 01:09:35,171
I’m wooing you with
my popcorn-making skills.

1333
01:09:35,345 --> 01:09:36,998
Really? (chuckles)

1334
01:09:37,173 --> 01:09:38,348
Oh...

1335
01:09:38,522 --> 01:09:41,133
Perfect combination
of butter and salt.

1336
01:09:43,570 --> 01:09:45,485
Hmm... Mm-hmm.
Uh-huh. Yup.

1337
01:09:46,486 --> 01:09:47,618
Where is everyone?

1338
01:09:47,792 --> 01:09:48,967
Oh, they’re
cleaning the floors.

1339
01:09:49,141 --> 01:09:50,795
But it takes
48 hours for it to dry,

1340
01:09:50,969 --> 01:09:52,666
so we have the theater
to ourselves.

1341
01:09:52,840 --> 01:09:54,538
What are we watching?

1342
01:09:54,712 --> 01:09:55,974
It’s a surprise.

1343
01:09:56,148 --> 01:09:57,454
Oh.

1344
01:09:57,628 --> 01:09:59,151
(chuckles)
My bad. (chuckles)

1345
01:09:59,325 --> 01:10:01,240
You ready, Efren?
(Efren) <i>It’s coming right up!</i>

1346
01:10:01,414 --> 01:10:02,676
<i>Hi, Clara.</i>
Hi, Efren.

1347
01:10:02,850 --> 01:10:04,156
Thank you.

1348
01:10:04,330 --> 01:10:06,332
(mellow music playing
over theater speakers)

1349
01:10:07,855 --> 01:10:11,729
I cannot get over
how much of a mess this is.

1350
01:10:11,903 --> 01:10:13,339
(chuckles)
It’s insane.

1351
01:10:13,513 --> 01:10:14,906
I just realized I got some
on the ceiling. (chuckles)

1352
01:10:15,080 --> 01:10:16,299
(Morgan laughing)
It’s everywhere.

1353
01:10:16,473 --> 01:10:17,822
Oh, wait, wait. Look at me.

1354
01:10:17,996 --> 01:10:19,693
I got you.

1355
01:10:19,867 --> 01:10:22,783
What is it? Oh, my God.
What do you think it is?

1356
01:10:24,045 --> 01:10:25,786
(both laughing)

1357
01:10:25,960 --> 01:10:27,310
How?

1358
01:10:27,484 --> 01:10:28,789
(continues laughing)
That’s insane!

1359
01:10:28,963 --> 01:10:30,182
It’s nice hearing you laugh.

1360
01:10:30,356 --> 01:10:32,445
You, too, Mr. Serious.

1361
01:10:32,619 --> 01:10:35,143
What?
Oh, come on. Jonah.

1362
01:10:35,318 --> 01:10:37,885
In school,
you were always so serious.

1363
01:10:38,059 --> 01:10:40,148
You were also mysterious.

1364
01:10:40,323 --> 01:10:42,673
With the glasses?
I mean, come on.

1365
01:10:42,847 --> 01:10:46,416
But I kind of made it a point
to notice everything about you.

1366
01:10:46,590 --> 01:10:48,156
Like what?

1367
01:10:48,331 --> 01:10:51,203
Um, I don’t know,
like your insane hatred

1368
01:10:51,377 --> 01:10:53,553
for watermelon Jolly Ranchers.

1369
01:10:54,293 --> 01:10:55,294
Weirdo.

1370
01:10:55,468 --> 01:10:57,470
They’re the best.

1371
01:10:57,644 --> 01:11:00,908
I didn’t hate them.
I actually love them.

1372
01:11:01,909 --> 01:11:03,694
I just saved them for you

1373
01:11:03,868 --> 01:11:06,174
because I know
they’re your favorite.

1374
01:11:09,874 --> 01:11:11,876
(Elijah cooing)

1375
01:11:14,139 --> 01:11:16,010
Gonna check on Elijah.

1376
01:11:16,184 --> 01:11:17,273
Morgan.

1377
01:11:18,143 --> 01:11:19,405
Jonah.

1378
01:11:21,668 --> 01:11:23,453
We’re both going through
a lot right now...

1379
01:11:23,627 --> 01:11:25,150
No, don’t do that.

1380
01:11:25,324 --> 01:11:27,283
And we’re feeling very
vulnerable and we are angry.

1381
01:11:27,457 --> 01:11:30,068
That’s not what this is.
I’ve wanted you since the day I met you.

1382
01:11:30,242 --> 01:11:32,331
(sighs)

1383
01:11:32,505 --> 01:11:34,768
My biggest regret is
not telling you how I felt

1384
01:11:34,942 --> 01:11:36,379
before Chris swooped in.

1385
01:11:36,553 --> 01:11:39,207
I should have fought
harder for you.

1386
01:11:39,382 --> 01:11:41,209
And I think
you felt the same.

1387
01:11:46,519 --> 01:11:47,738
Yeah, but...

1388
01:11:47,912 --> 01:11:49,348
it doesn’t matter.

1389
01:11:49,522 --> 01:11:50,828
(choked up) It doesn’t matter
what I felt then,

1390
01:11:51,002 --> 01:11:52,090
it doesn’t matter
what I feel now.

1391
01:11:52,264 --> 01:11:54,135
This is my life now.

1392
01:11:54,310 --> 01:11:55,963
Clara’s my world, that’s it.

1393
01:11:56,137 --> 01:12:00,054
This isn’t about Clara.
Everything is about Clara.

1394
01:12:01,621 --> 01:12:03,406
And protecting her
from the truth?

1395
01:12:03,580 --> 01:12:04,755
Yes.

1396
01:12:05,799 --> 01:12:07,410
And as a matter of fact,

1397
01:12:08,846 --> 01:12:10,413
take these with you.

1398
01:12:10,587 --> 01:12:12,676
I don’t want her
to find them, okay?

1399
01:12:12,850 --> 01:12:16,244
You’ll get there, but you
do not know what it is like

1400
01:12:16,419 --> 01:12:19,160
to put somebody else
before yourself.

1401
01:12:19,335 --> 01:12:21,685
I’ve been doing that
for 17 years.

1402
01:12:25,732 --> 01:12:27,560
I do know what it’s like.

1403
01:12:27,734 --> 01:12:29,693
Okay? That’s why I left
all those years ago.

1404
01:12:29,867 --> 01:12:32,826
It’s because I had respect
for them. For you.

1405
01:12:33,000 --> 01:12:35,481
Leaving
was the hardest thing I have ever done.

1406
01:12:35,655 --> 01:12:38,179
Okay?
I left because I loved you.

1407
01:12:40,312 --> 01:12:41,922
I still love you.

1408
01:12:47,232 --> 01:12:49,103
What about Jenny?

1409
01:12:49,277 --> 01:12:51,192
Did you love her or...?

1410
01:12:51,845 --> 01:12:52,846
I did.

1411
01:12:53,020 --> 01:12:55,240
And I wanted
to do right by her.

1412
01:12:55,414 --> 01:12:57,677
But she didn’t
do right by me.

1413
01:12:57,851 --> 01:12:59,200
And neither did
my best friend.

1414
01:13:00,419 --> 01:13:01,551
But I’m not gonna
let their betrayal

1415
01:13:01,725 --> 01:13:03,770
dictate the rest of my life

1416
01:13:03,944 --> 01:13:05,381
and you shouldn’t, either...

1417
01:13:06,425 --> 01:13:10,081
(Elijah cooing, fussing)

1418
01:13:13,214 --> 01:13:15,347
<i>Cher, get in here.</i>
<i>What’s up, Daddy?</i>

1419
01:13:15,521 --> 01:13:17,523
<i>What the hell is that?</i>
<i>A dress.</i>

1420
01:13:17,697 --> 01:13:19,525
<i>Says who?</i>
<i>Calvin Klein.</i>

1421
01:13:19,699 --> 01:13:21,179
<i>It looks like underwear.</i>

1422
01:13:21,353 --> 01:13:22,789
<i>Go upstairs</i>
<i>and put something over it.</i>

1423
01:13:22,963 --> 01:13:24,400
Just so you know,

1424
01:13:25,488 --> 01:13:27,403
I am a virgin.

1425
01:13:28,665 --> 01:13:30,623
I know a cure for that.

1426
01:13:31,276 --> 01:13:32,495
(chuckles)

1427
01:13:32,669 --> 01:13:34,932
(chuckles)
No, I’m glad you told me.

1428
01:13:35,106 --> 01:13:37,543
And just so you’re aware,
I’m in no hurry.

1429
01:13:37,717 --> 01:13:42,069
I’m having a wonderful time
not having sex with you.

1430
01:13:42,243 --> 01:13:44,245
(chuckles) Okay.

1431
01:13:46,813 --> 01:13:50,687
Good.
Because I think that

1432
01:13:50,861 --> 01:13:53,341
we should wait to have sex
until prom night.

1433
01:13:55,169 --> 01:14:00,000
Cheesy? Sure,
but what do you say?

1434
01:14:00,174 --> 01:14:02,089
I mean,
shouldn’t I ask you first?

1435
01:14:02,263 --> 01:14:05,832
Yeah, sure,
but no lame promposals.

1436
01:14:07,051 --> 01:14:09,836
Well, yeah,
I hate those things anyway.

1437
01:14:11,447 --> 01:14:15,451
("This Far South" playing)

1438
01:14:24,982 --> 01:14:27,985
("This Far South"
continues playing)

1439
01:14:33,294 --> 01:14:37,124
♪ <i>You remind me</i> ♪

1440
01:14:37,298 --> 01:14:41,607
♪ <i>Of every single</i>
<i>Dogwood tree</i> ♪

1441
01:14:41,781 --> 01:14:45,524
♪ <i>When I tried to reach out</i> ♪

1442
01:14:45,698 --> 01:14:51,095
♪ <i>I never see you</i>
<i>This far south no more</i> ♪

1443
01:14:51,269 --> 01:14:53,271
(Lexie) There we go.

1444
01:14:53,445 --> 01:14:54,968
Is this gonna wash off?
Is this--

1445
01:14:55,142 --> 01:14:56,622
Wait, are you getting it?
Yeah, I’m getting it all.

1446
01:14:56,796 --> 01:14:59,277
(Efren) No, don’t do that.
(chuckles)

1447
01:14:59,451 --> 01:15:01,453
Oh, my gosh, he’s so cute!

1448
01:15:01,627 --> 01:15:03,499
♪ <i>Any less than all of me</i> ♪

1449
01:15:03,673 --> 01:15:08,155
♪ <i>But that won’t work out</i> ♪

1450
01:15:08,329 --> 01:15:10,070
(whirring)

1451
01:15:10,244 --> 01:15:13,204
♪ <i>If words can’t fall</i>
<i>Out my mouth no more</i> ♪

1452
01:15:16,947 --> 01:15:18,252
♪ <i>Angel</i> ♪

1453
01:15:18,426 --> 01:15:19,384
(clacks)
(exclaims)

1454
01:15:19,558 --> 01:15:21,255
♪ <i>Walk me</i> ♪

1455
01:15:21,429 --> 01:15:23,127
<i>Through your garden</i> ♪

1456
01:15:23,301 --> 01:15:24,824
(loud thud, shattering)
(exclaims)

1457
01:15:24,998 --> 01:15:26,478
♪ <i>Won’t you please again?</i> ♪

1458
01:15:27,261 --> 01:15:28,262
(sighs)

1459
01:15:28,436 --> 01:15:29,916
Get me the hell out of here.

1460
01:15:30,090 --> 01:15:33,703
♪ <i>The nerves</i>
<i>Inside my heart</i> ♪

1461
01:15:33,877 --> 01:15:38,011
♪ <i>In Germantown tonight</i> ♪

1462
01:15:38,185 --> 01:15:40,361
♪ <i>I’m learning</i> ♪

1463
01:15:40,536 --> 01:15:43,321
♪ <i>That it’s not good to fly</i> ♪

1464
01:15:43,495 --> 01:15:46,193
(indistinct chatter)

1465
01:15:47,325 --> 01:15:49,501
♪ <i>I’ve chosen</i> ♪

1466
01:15:49,675 --> 01:15:52,373
♪ <i>The habit</i>
<i>That I’m dropping</i> ♪

1467
01:15:52,548 --> 01:15:54,288
(song continues playing)

1468
