"Real Housewife" show.

1714
01:30:02,527 --> 01:30:04,747
Drama and scandal
at every turn.

1715
01:30:04,921 --> 01:30:07,793
As for me, I will be
skipping season two,

1716
01:30:07,967 --> 01:30:11,231
because I got accepted
into UNCSA’s drama program.

1717
01:30:12,972 --> 01:30:13,886
What?

1718
01:30:14,060 --> 01:30:15,453
Yay!

1719
01:30:15,627 --> 01:30:16,976
Cheers to me.

1720
01:30:17,150 --> 01:30:18,761
Okay, I can’t do this.
Thank you, Mrs. Grant.

1721
01:30:18,935 --> 01:30:20,937
Thank you, Mr. Sullivan.
Enjoy dinner.

1722
01:30:21,807 --> 01:30:23,287
Miller?

1723
01:30:24,331 --> 01:30:25,376
Clara?

1724
01:30:31,600 --> 01:30:33,036
(sighs)

1725
01:30:33,210 --> 01:30:34,777
Lexie, I think you should
head home right about now.

1726
01:30:34,951 --> 01:30:36,692
I’m staying over,
remember?

1727
01:30:38,041 --> 01:30:40,783
We’ve all got to ride
this shit out together.

1728
01:30:40,957 --> 01:30:43,438
Miller, hey, wait! Hey!

1729
01:30:43,612 --> 01:30:45,440
When were you gonna
tell me you got in?

1730
01:30:47,180 --> 01:30:48,617
(voice breaks)
I only found out today.

1731
01:30:48,791 --> 01:30:51,097
Congratulations.
I’m on the wait list.

1732
01:30:51,271 --> 01:30:53,535
Shit. Miller.
No!

1733
01:30:53,709 --> 01:30:56,189
You keep using me
to piss your mom off, and I’m done with it.

1734
01:30:56,363 --> 01:30:58,496
Hey, hey, you’re done?

1735
01:30:58,670 --> 01:31:01,673
Okay, so what, you’re just gonna sleep
with me last night and then dump me?

1736
01:31:01,847 --> 01:31:03,327
No, you don’t get
to throw that in my face.

1737
01:31:03,501 --> 01:31:05,460
I was the one taken advantage
of last night, not you.

1738
01:31:05,634 --> 01:31:07,026
I’m sorry. I screwed up.

1739
01:31:07,200 --> 01:31:09,420
I mean, they disrespected

1740
01:31:09,594 --> 01:31:11,509
the two most important
people in my life,

1741
01:31:11,683 --> 01:31:13,946
and I’m supposed to
sit here and pretend like I’m fine with it?

1742
01:31:14,120 --> 01:31:16,688
When are you gonna realize
you’re not the only one with problems?

1743
01:31:16,862 --> 01:31:18,429
Okay, Gramps
starts chemo next week,

1744
01:31:18,603 --> 01:31:20,170
and you’re gonna go off
to some amazing school,

1745
01:31:20,344 --> 01:31:22,912
and I’m gonna be stuck here
in Nowheresville.

1746
01:31:24,174 --> 01:31:25,218
(engine starts)

1747
01:31:27,786 --> 01:31:29,919
(sobs)

1748
01:31:35,054 --> 01:31:36,491
God.

1749
01:31:36,665 --> 01:31:38,144
(sniffles)

1750
01:31:39,015 --> 01:31:40,059
Hey.

1751
01:31:41,321 --> 01:31:45,543
So it seems like now
is the perfect time...

1752
01:31:45,717 --> 01:31:46,762
(bottles clink)
...to give you

1753
01:31:46,936 --> 01:31:48,764
your birthday present.

1754
01:31:48,938 --> 01:31:49,982
(chuckles)

1755
01:31:51,680 --> 01:31:53,159
Let’s get out of here.
(sniffles)

1756
01:31:53,333 --> 01:31:54,987
What? Wait.
Where are we going?

1757
01:31:55,161 --> 01:31:56,859
I want to see my dad
and Aunt Jenny.

1758
01:31:57,033 --> 01:31:58,513
(engine starts)

1759
01:32:06,738 --> 01:32:08,348
Did they really just take off?

1760
01:32:08,523 --> 01:32:10,525
(owl hooting)

1761
01:32:12,483 --> 01:32:14,354
I miss you, Aunt Jenny.

1762
01:32:14,529 --> 01:32:16,531
We miss you so much.
Mmm...

1763
01:32:17,140 --> 01:32:18,271
Oh.

1764
01:32:20,752 --> 01:32:22,667
You were like my best friend.

1765
01:32:23,668 --> 01:32:24,843
It was...
Go ahead.

1766
01:32:25,017 --> 01:32:26,541
No, you know what I mean.

1767
01:32:26,715 --> 01:32:28,934
Yeah. No, I get it.
She was cool as shit.

1768
01:32:29,108 --> 01:32:31,850
Mmm...
Pour one out for the--

1769
01:32:32,024 --> 01:32:33,896
Yeah.
Yeah. Drink up, girl.

1770
01:32:34,070 --> 01:32:35,898
Good call.
She liked this stuff.

1771
01:32:36,072 --> 01:32:38,596
Yeah. I do, too.
Mmm...

1772
01:32:39,989 --> 01:32:41,904
Let’s, um...
Let’s go see my dad.

1773
01:32:42,078 --> 01:32:43,470
Yeah, lead the way.

1774
01:32:43,645 --> 01:32:45,864
(both chattering indistinctly)

1775
01:33:03,099 --> 01:33:07,320
(yawning) Can you believe
I am dating Efren?

1776
01:33:10,019 --> 01:33:13,457
Can you believe I lost
my virginity to Miller?

1777
01:33:13,631 --> 01:33:15,938
(snickers) No.

1778
01:33:16,112 --> 01:33:19,594
Wait. And like what,
are you guys broken up now?

1779
01:33:23,119 --> 01:33:25,164
(sighs) I don’t even know.

1780
01:33:25,338 --> 01:33:27,166
Hmm...

1781
01:33:27,340 --> 01:33:28,733
I mean,
I’d break up with me.

1782
01:33:28,907 --> 01:33:30,517
I mean, it’s, like...
(voice cracks)

1783
01:33:34,478 --> 01:33:35,697
I don’t know.

1784
01:33:38,525 --> 01:33:41,137
Part of me
did it to hurt her, and then I just...

1785
01:33:42,660 --> 01:33:44,401
ended up hurting him.

1786
01:33:46,751 --> 01:33:49,580
Like a walking disaster.

1787
01:33:59,372 --> 01:34:01,853
(crying)
All of this is my fault.

1788
01:34:03,333 --> 01:34:07,293
(sobbing) I’m so sorry, Dad.

1789
01:34:14,257 --> 01:34:16,868
(Lexie grunts softly)
(Morgan) Clara?

1790
01:34:19,131 --> 01:34:20,698
We need to talk.

1791
01:34:22,482 --> 01:34:23,658
(retches)

1792
01:34:29,141 --> 01:34:30,621
Bye, car.

1793
01:34:32,188 --> 01:34:34,277
(toilet flushing)

1794
01:34:37,236 --> 01:34:39,456
I’m never drinking again.

1795
01:34:40,979 --> 01:34:42,589
It’s all my fault.

1796
01:34:42,764 --> 01:34:46,071
Aww... You got angry
at your mom and you got drunk.

1797
01:34:46,245 --> 01:34:49,771
It happens to almost
every teenager in the world.

1798
01:34:49,945 --> 01:34:51,511
The accident.

1799
01:34:52,904 --> 01:34:54,819
It was my fault.

1800
01:34:56,908 --> 01:34:58,127
What?

1801
01:35:10,443 --> 01:35:13,838
(sighs) My head.
Yeah, that’s gonna hurt. A lot.

1802
01:35:14,012 --> 01:35:16,145
Here, sit down. Take this.

1803
01:35:30,812 --> 01:35:33,075
Last night you said something,

1804
01:35:33,249 --> 01:35:34,772
and I wanted
to ask you about it.

1805
01:35:34,946 --> 01:35:37,035
Might have been
the wine talking, but...

1806
01:35:39,864 --> 01:35:41,779
you said you...

1807
01:35:41,953 --> 01:35:43,650
blame yourself
for the accident?

1808
01:35:43,825 --> 01:35:46,044
Why would you think that?

1809
01:35:46,218 --> 01:35:47,437
I don’t...

1810
01:35:51,223 --> 01:35:52,964
know. (sobs)

1811
01:35:53,138 --> 01:35:55,924
(sobbing)
I mean, it’s my fault that they’re dead.

1812
01:35:56,098 --> 01:35:57,752
What?

1813
01:36:00,102 --> 01:36:03,845
I mean, I didn’t know
that she was driving.

1814
01:36:04,671 --> 01:36:06,761
And I was just...

1815
01:36:08,501 --> 01:36:10,547
text bombing Jenny,
and now they’re...

1816
01:36:10,721 --> 01:36:13,419
Oh, my God, sweetheart, sweetheart,
she was not driving.

1817
01:36:13,593 --> 01:36:15,595
Your dad was driving.

1818
01:36:15,770 --> 01:36:18,903
It is so not your fault.
It is not your fault.

1819
01:36:24,822 --> 01:36:26,432
What aren’t you telling me?

1820
01:36:27,520 --> 01:36:30,349
Why were they
really together?

1821
01:36:32,003 --> 01:36:34,049
I didn’t want to tell you this,
because...

1822
01:36:35,920 --> 01:36:38,314
I would never want you
to think less of them.

1823
01:36:39,750 --> 01:36:41,230
But your father

1824
01:36:41,404 --> 01:36:43,493
and Aunt Jenny, they were...

1825
01:36:45,190 --> 01:36:46,713
Having an affair?

1826
01:36:51,370 --> 01:36:53,024
For how long?

1827
01:36:53,198 --> 01:36:56,506
A long time, apparently.

1828
01:36:56,680 --> 01:36:58,987
But you didn’t think
to tell me that?

1829
01:36:59,161 --> 01:37:01,293
I was trying to protect
your memories of them

1830
01:37:01,467 --> 01:37:05,036
because your dad made some
really big mistakes, yes,

1831
01:37:05,210 --> 01:37:07,647
but he also did a lot right.

1832
01:37:07,822 --> 01:37:09,388
And the same goes
for Aunt Jenny.

1833
01:37:09,562 --> 01:37:11,260
And they loved you so much.

1834
01:37:11,434 --> 01:37:13,697
You and Jonah, I saw you.

1835
01:37:13,871 --> 01:37:18,441
That was the first time
we have ever kissed, I swear.

1836
01:37:18,615 --> 01:37:20,530
I would never have done that
to your father

1837
01:37:20,704 --> 01:37:23,315
or Aunt Jenny,
especially to you. Never.

1838
01:37:24,795 --> 01:37:26,362
But they did it to you.

1839
01:37:33,586 --> 01:37:34,805
Yeah.

1840
01:37:38,287 --> 01:37:40,680
Do you regret marrying him?

1841
01:37:40,855 --> 01:37:43,161
Oh, no, no, I don’t.
I couldn’t.

1842
01:37:45,598 --> 01:37:49,385
I would go back and do it all
the exact same way if I could.

1843
01:37:49,559 --> 01:37:52,083
Because if even one thing
happened differently,

1844
01:37:52,257 --> 01:37:54,172
you wouldn’t be here,

1845
01:37:54,346 --> 01:38:00,004
and you are the best thing
in my life for miles.

1846
01:38:01,571 --> 01:38:06,924
Clara, there is no life that
I want that you are not in.

1847
01:38:07,794 --> 01:38:09,753
(sniffles)

1848
01:38:09,927 --> 01:38:11,798
(cell phone buzzes)

1849
01:38:19,110 --> 01:38:20,807
You deserve to be happy.

1850
01:38:24,115 --> 01:38:25,725
No regrets, right?

1851
01:38:27,727 --> 01:38:30,034
We both deserve
to be happy, okay?

1852
01:38:38,390 --> 01:38:40,784
(Lexie) Oh, my God,
what time is it?

1853
01:38:40,958 --> 01:38:43,221
Oh, Clara, we’re gonna
be late for school.

1854
01:38:43,395 --> 01:38:45,223
(Morgan and Clara)
It’s the weekend!

1855
01:38:45,397 --> 01:38:46,703
Oh...

1856
01:38:46,877 --> 01:38:48,923
(chuckles) Lexie.

1857
01:38:55,451 --> 01:38:58,933
(Clara) <i>I’m sorry. </i>
<i>I was wrong about everything.</i>

1858
01:39:01,848 --> 01:39:04,199
<i>There’s so much </i>
<i>I need to tell you.</i>

1859
01:39:06,070 --> 01:39:08,029
Lame, Clara.

1860
01:39:10,770 --> 01:39:12,337
(cell phone chimes)

1861
01:39:17,255 --> 01:39:20,563
(Miller) <i>I’m sorry, too.</i>
<i>How soon can I see you?</i>

1862
01:39:20,737 --> 01:39:21,956
How can I help you?

1863
01:39:22,130 --> 01:39:23,609
(man)
Can I get some Gummy Bears?

1864
01:39:23,783 --> 01:39:24,828
Yeah.Efren.

1865
01:39:25,002 --> 01:39:26,264
We--

1866
01:39:26,438 --> 01:39:27,700
Efren!

1867
01:39:27,874 --> 01:39:29,528
Um, sorry.
Where is he?

1868
01:39:29,702 --> 01:39:30,965
He’s... He’s...

1869
01:39:31,139 --> 01:39:32,967
Movie about to start, man.

1870
01:39:33,141 --> 01:39:34,838
Hey, Miller, I’ve got Clara here,
and she’s headed your way.

1871
01:39:35,012 --> 01:39:36,971
No, she’s running.
She’s sprinting.

1872
01:39:37,145 --> 01:39:39,147
Excuse me.
(indistinct chattering)

1873
01:39:54,945 --> 01:39:56,338
(laughing)

1874
01:40:09,264 --> 01:40:11,266
(thunder rumbling)
(rain pattering)

1875
01:40:35,029 --> 01:40:36,726
Always miss one.

1876
01:40:51,219 --> 01:40:54,831
("Splits Are Parted"
playing)

1877
01:41:03,622 --> 01:41:05,624
We did get it wrong.

1878
01:41:07,496 --> 01:41:09,063
It should have been us.

1879
01:41:10,586 --> 01:41:11,978
I love you.

1880
01:41:14,720 --> 01:41:19,203
♪ <i>Splits are parted </i>
<i>Since we parted in April</i> ♪

1881
01:41:19,377 --> 01:41:22,859
♪ <i>Go to bed now</i>
<i>Sing me a song</i> ♪

1882
01:41:24,034 --> 01:41:28,386
♪ <i>Gonna see me going inside</i> ♪

1883
01:41:28,560 --> 01:41:32,260
♪ <i>Gonna see me</i>
<i>Going inside</i> ♪

1884
01:41:32,434 --> 01:41:34,349
(song continues playing)
(chuckling) Thank you.

1885
01:41:34,523 --> 01:41:38,744
♪ <i>Oh, I could love you</i> ♪

1886
01:41:41,617 --> 01:41:47,884
♪ <i>Oh, then it’d be easy</i> ♪

1887
01:41:50,887 --> 01:41:57,328
♪ <i>Oh, I’ll come find you</i> ♪

1888
01:42:00,201 --> 01:42:07,121
♪ <i>Oh, then it’d be easy</i> ♪

1889
01:42:09,688 --> 01:42:10,950
(song ends)

1890
01:42:11,125 --> 01:42:13,301
(Clara) Yeah. No. Sure.
(cell phone ringing)

1891
01:42:15,172 --> 01:42:16,478
Thank you.

1892
01:42:16,652 --> 01:42:18,349
Hi, Mom.
(Morgan) <i>Almost done?</i>

1893
01:42:18,523 --> 01:42:19,872
Yeah, I’m just wrapping up.

1894
01:42:20,046 --> 01:42:21,396
(Morgan) <i>Great. </i>
<i>Want to watch a movie tonight?</i>

1895
01:42:21,570 --> 01:42:23,180
Mm-hmm. I’m on my way.

1896
01:42:23,354 --> 01:42:25,313
(Morgan) <i>See you soon,</i>
<i>Clare Bear.</i>

1897
01:42:25,487 --> 01:42:26,923
(Lexie) I think
it’s more than enough.

1898
01:42:27,097 --> 01:42:28,664
We’re filling two whole bowls.

1899
01:42:28,838 --> 01:42:30,492
That’s a whole bag of popcorn.
(Morgan) Are you sure?

1900
01:42:30,666 --> 01:42:31,841
(Lexie) Yeah, absolutely.

1901
01:42:32,015 --> 01:42:33,408
I’m back.

1902
01:42:33,582 --> 01:42:35,105
Oh, hello.

1903
01:42:35,279 --> 01:42:36,846
Hi.

1904
01:42:37,020 --> 01:42:39,936
What’s going on?
(Lexie) A surprise, bitch!

1905
01:42:40,110 --> 01:42:41,329
Lexie.
(Lexie) Sorry.

1906
01:42:41,503 --> 01:42:42,765
Hello.

1907
01:42:42,939 --> 01:42:45,202
(Lexie) Come with me.Where?

1908
01:42:46,551 --> 01:42:47,900
Oh... (laughing)
Close your eyes.

1909
01:42:48,074 --> 01:42:49,772
Okay, just be careful, honey.
What is happening?

1910
01:42:49,946 --> 01:42:51,643
Is this necessary?
Yes!

1911
01:42:51,817 --> 01:42:54,690
I’m gonna switch my hand. Okay.
(continues laughing) Hello?

1912
01:42:54,864 --> 01:42:57,519
And... Okay, stop!
Or else you’re gonna fall off.

1913
01:42:58,433 --> 01:43:00,130
And... Ta-da!

1914
01:43:00,304 --> 01:43:01,697
(chuckles)

1915
01:43:01,871 --> 01:43:03,264
What is this?

1916
01:43:03,438 --> 01:43:05,179
Oh, nothing.
(Lexie giggles)

1917
01:43:06,267 --> 01:43:07,268
Miller?

1918
01:43:08,617 --> 01:43:10,009
(Morgan) We did it.
We pulled it off.

1919
01:43:10,184 --> 01:43:11,968
What are you doing?

1920
01:43:12,142 --> 01:43:15,798
Humor me. Grab a seat.
Grab some popcorn! (Clara chuckles)

1921
01:43:15,972 --> 01:43:17,669
Hello.

1922
01:43:17,843 --> 01:43:18,931
I know, right?

1923
01:43:19,105 --> 01:43:20,281
He’s starting.
Is it starting?

1924
01:43:20,455 --> 01:43:21,630
(Miller) Yeah.
Is this fine? Yeah, okay.

1925
01:43:21,804 --> 01:43:23,109
(indistinct chattering)

1926
01:43:23,284 --> 01:43:24,807
Squeeze.
Okay.

1927
01:43:24,981 --> 01:43:26,852
(Efren) Yeah, okay.

1928
01:43:27,026 --> 01:43:30,073
(Miller) Okay, I want
to start off with saying,

1929
01:43:30,247 --> 01:43:34,077
thank you, everyone,
for being here tonight. Um...

1930
01:43:34,251 --> 01:43:38,124
As we all know, I was on
the wait list for film school.

1931
01:43:39,343 --> 01:43:40,388
And, um...

1932
01:43:42,564 --> 01:43:43,652
I got in.

1933
01:43:43,826 --> 01:43:46,437
(all cheering)
(Gramps) Attaboy!

1934
01:43:46,611 --> 01:43:48,657
I’ll be darned. Good for you.

1935
01:43:48,831 --> 01:43:53,792
But I’m going to defer and
stick around here for a while

1936
01:43:53,966 --> 01:43:56,839
and take care of my gramps
the next couple rounds of chemo.

1937
01:43:57,013 --> 01:43:59,842
That’s a bunch of horseshit.

1938
01:44:00,016 --> 01:44:02,279
Boy, I’ve been telling you
since you were a little fart

1939
01:44:02,453 --> 01:44:03,846
you could have my air.

1940
01:44:04,020 --> 01:44:05,326
My air rights.

1941
01:44:05,500 --> 01:44:06,936
I bought them
when your gram and me

1942
01:44:07,110 --> 01:44:08,546
lived in New York,
back in the day.

1943
01:44:08,720 --> 01:44:10,113
What are you talking about?

1944
01:44:10,287 --> 01:44:14,422
Well, in big cities,
you can buy the rights to air.

1945
01:44:14,596 --> 01:44:16,946
So that, you know,
people can’t build

1946
01:44:17,120 --> 01:44:20,036
in front of your building
or on top of you.

1947
01:44:20,210 --> 01:44:24,345
And I’ve owned a little piece
in Union Square worth about...

1948
01:44:24,519 --> 01:44:25,911
I don’t know,
half a million dollars

1949
01:44:26,085 --> 01:44:27,609
last time I checked.
(gasps)

1950
01:44:27,783 --> 01:44:30,699
But the point is we got
enough money to afford

1951
01:44:30,873 --> 01:44:35,660
any home health care
if necessary and your tuition.

1952
01:44:35,834 --> 01:44:37,140
(chuckles)

1953
01:44:37,314 --> 01:44:39,751
Uh, this is...

1954
01:44:39,925 --> 01:44:44,452
amazing news
that we’ll talk about later.

1955
01:44:44,626 --> 01:44:46,323
Sorry. My bad.

1956
01:44:46,497 --> 01:44:47,716
(Morgan laughs)
But tonight

1957
01:44:47,890 --> 01:44:49,587
is about you, Clara.

1958
01:44:50,893 --> 01:44:52,111
And this movie is for you.

1959
01:44:52,286 --> 01:44:55,680
And naturally, you’re the star.

1960
01:44:56,812 --> 01:44:58,640
Efren, hit it.
(Morgan gasps)

1961
01:44:59,815 --> 01:45:01,207
(Gramps chuckles)

1962
01:45:04,602 --> 01:45:06,387
<i>It’s been 14 years, Mama.</i>

1963
01:45:07,126 --> 01:45:08,867
<i>I’m dead.</i>

1964
01:45:09,041 --> 01:45:12,001
<i>You’re a grandmother, Mama.</i>
<i>Don’t you remember?</i>

1965
01:45:12,175 --> 01:45:14,046
(Miller over speakers) <i>Hey, </i>
<i>Efren, take the camera from me.</i>

1966
01:45:14,220 --> 01:45:16,397
(Efren over speakers)
<i>Yeah, got it, got it.</i>

1967
01:45:16,571 --> 01:45:18,616
I directed this part. This...

1968
01:45:18,790 --> 01:45:20,923
Shut up. She’s acting.
Okay. Sorry. Sorry.

1969
01:45:21,097 --> 01:45:24,361
<i>Look at my grandson.</i>
<i>I think he’s in love.</i>

1970
01:45:24,535 --> 01:45:25,754
(thuds)
(chuckles)

1971
01:45:25,928 --> 01:45:28,757
(Clara) <i>Let us</i>
<i>look at one another.</i>

1972
01:45:28,931 --> 01:45:30,411
<i>What’s her name?</i>

1973
01:45:30,585 --> 01:45:33,109
(Clara) <i>I can’t go on.</i>
<i>I never realized...</i>

1974
01:45:33,283 --> 01:45:34,328
<i>Uh, Clara.</i>

1975
01:45:35,024 --> 01:45:36,068
<i>Clara Grant.</i>

1976
01:45:38,114 --> 01:45:40,159
<i>Take me back.</i>

1977
01:45:40,334 --> 01:45:42,161
<i>Up the hill to my grave.</i>

1978
01:45:43,337 --> 01:45:45,121
<i>Oh, earth,</i>
<i>you’re too wonderful</i>

1979
01:45:45,295 --> 01:45:47,863
<i>for anybody</i>
<i>to actually realize you.</i>

1980
01:45:48,037 --> 01:45:51,693
<i>Do any human beings</i>
<i>actually realize life</i> <i>while they live it?</i>

1981
01:45:52,824 --> 01:45:55,305
<i>Every... Every minute?</i>

1982
01:45:57,655 --> 01:45:59,962
<i>Hey, Clara, um...</i>

1983
01:46:00,136 --> 01:46:01,833
<i>I know you said </i>
<i>no lame promposals,</i>

1984
01:46:02,007 --> 01:46:04,009
<i>but I kind of already started </i>
<i>this before you said that.</i>

1985
01:46:04,183 --> 01:46:06,055
<i>So I hope you like it.</i>

1986
01:46:06,229 --> 01:46:10,668
(sighs) <i>Clara... I think you </i>
<i>should go to prom with me.</i>

1987
01:46:14,106 --> 01:46:16,326
<i>What’s up, dude?</i>
(Clara chuckling) <i>Hey!</i>

1988
01:46:16,500 --> 01:46:17,849
(squeals)
(Miller chuckles)

1989
01:46:18,023 --> 01:46:19,677
<i>You’re a little preoccupied </i>
<i>with some goats,</i>

1990
01:46:19,851 --> 01:46:21,679
<i>but I still think you should </i>
<i>go to prom with me.</i>

1991
01:46:21,853 --> 01:46:23,551
<i>Maybe don’t bring the goats.</i>

1992
01:46:23,725 --> 01:46:26,249
Those are my goats!
(laughter)

1993
01:46:26,423 --> 01:46:27,685
Those are mine.

1994
01:46:27,859 --> 01:46:30,166
<i>Clara, I think you </i>
<i>should go to prom with me.</i>

1995
01:46:30,340 --> 01:46:32,211
(scoffing) <i>Yeah, right.</i>
<i>Whatever, dude.</i>

1996
01:46:32,864 --> 01:46:34,431
(laughter)

1997
01:46:34,605 --> 01:46:37,521
(exhales) <i>Okay, so here’s </i>
<i>the thing, Clara Grant.</i>

1998
01:46:37,695 --> 01:46:40,655
<i>You just drove by and I know </i>
<i>you saw me standing here.</i>

1999
01:46:40,829 --> 01:46:42,657
<i>I do have a girlfriend, but...</i>

2000
01:46:44,485 --> 01:46:46,138
<i>all I think about </i>
<i>is you, so...</i>

2001
01:46:46,312 --> 01:46:48,445
<i>if you turn around</i>
<i>and offer me a ride,</i>

2002
01:46:48,619 --> 01:46:50,578
<i>I’ll take that as a sign</i>
<i>and I’ll break up</i> <i>with my girlfriend</i>

2003
01:46:50,752 --> 01:46:53,494
<i>and I’ll eventually</i>
<i>ask you out.</i> <i>But if you don’t...</i>

2004
01:46:53,668 --> 01:46:56,453
<i>I’ll just assume </i>
<i>that we weren’t meant to be.</i>

2005
01:47:00,326 --> 01:47:01,371
<i>You’re coming back.</i>

2006
01:47:02,067 --> 01:47:03,417
(gasps)

2007
01:47:06,158 --> 01:47:09,074
<i>Okay, what do you say,</i>
<i>Clara Grant?</i>

2008
01:47:09,248 --> 01:47:10,641
<i>Will you go to prom with me?</i>

2009
01:47:12,164 --> 01:47:14,123
Of course I will.

2010
01:47:14,297 --> 01:47:16,908
Oh... Yay!
Oh, wow.

2011
01:47:17,082 --> 01:47:18,867
(applause)

2012
01:47:19,041 --> 01:47:21,739
Yay.Oh, yay!

2013
01:47:21,913 --> 01:47:23,698
(Lexie) Oh, my goodness!

2014
01:47:26,048 --> 01:47:28,442
I should have just
made you a video. (chuckles)

2015
01:47:28,616 --> 01:47:30,052
Could have saved us
a lot of time.

2016
01:47:30,226 --> 01:47:31,662
It’s so true.

2017
01:47:35,013 --> 01:47:36,537
Um...

2018
01:47:36,711 --> 01:47:39,540
I am so sorry to interrupt.
Miller, that was adorable.

2019
01:47:39,714 --> 01:47:41,106
Thank you, Mrs. Grant.

2020
01:47:41,280 --> 01:47:43,805
Do you mind if I steal
your prom date for a second?

2021
01:47:43,979 --> 01:47:45,371
(chuckles)
Go ahead.

2022
01:47:46,416 --> 01:47:47,809
(Morgan) Oh, my gosh!

2023
01:47:47,983 --> 01:47:50,594
I’m not gonna
keep you for long.

2024
01:47:50,768 --> 01:47:54,380
I just wanted to say that
watching you on that screen...

2025
01:47:55,338 --> 01:47:56,861
Clara, you’re so talented.

2026
01:47:57,035 --> 01:48:00,952
And so... fearless.

2027
01:48:01,126 --> 01:48:04,303
And I don’t want my fears
to hold you back. Okay?

2028
01:48:04,478 --> 01:48:07,219
I want you to follow your passions
wherever they take you.

2029
01:48:07,393 --> 01:48:10,832
I want you to ignore
everything and everyone. Even me.

2030
01:48:11,746 --> 01:48:13,356
Mostly.(chuckles)

2031
01:48:13,530 --> 01:48:15,837
I’m just blown away
by the person you are.

2032
01:48:18,013 --> 01:48:20,319
I’m only who I am
because of you.

2033
01:48:21,886 --> 01:48:23,932
You got me this far.
(chuckles)

2034
01:48:24,106 --> 01:48:28,197
My God,
such a sweet thing to say.

2035
01:48:28,371 --> 01:48:30,112
I’m proud of you, too, Mom.

2036
01:48:30,286 --> 01:48:31,505
Thank you.

2037
01:48:33,942 --> 01:48:35,247
I love you.
I love you.

2038
01:48:35,421 --> 01:48:36,858
Jinx! (chuckles)
Jinx!

2039
01:48:37,032 --> 01:48:38,729
(Morgan) Now I’ll make you
buy me a soda

2040
01:48:38,903 --> 01:48:40,905
because
it’s a very special day.

2041
01:48:41,079 --> 01:48:43,299
I brought
your prom date back.

2042
01:48:43,473 --> 01:48:46,345
("Everywhere, Everything"
playing)

2043
01:49:02,448 --> 01:49:05,190
(Clara) Got it? No?
(Miller) Yeah. (grunts)

2044
01:49:11,501 --> 01:49:13,938
(phone line ringing)

2045
01:49:14,112 --> 01:49:17,115
(man) <i>Roman’s Pizza. Will this </i>
<i>be for takeout or delivery?</i>

2046
01:49:17,289 --> 01:49:18,290
Uh, delivery.

2047
01:49:18,464 --> 01:49:21,293
(chuckles)
Definitely delivery.

2048
01:49:21,467 --> 01:49:23,687
(man) <i>All right, sir. </i>
<i>Ready when you are.</i>

2049
01:49:23,861 --> 01:49:25,384
<i>What can I get you?</i>

2050
01:49:25,559 --> 01:49:27,822
Do you guys
do pineapple on pizza?

2051
01:49:27,996 --> 01:49:29,693
(chuckles)

2052
01:49:29,867 --> 01:49:31,565
("Everywhere, Everything"
continues playing)

2053
01:49:31,739 --> 01:49:34,263
♪ <i>Everywhere, everything</i> ♪

2054
01:49:34,437 --> 01:49:38,223
♪ <i>I wanna love you till we’re </i>
<i>Food for the worms to eat</i> ♪

2055
01:49:38,397 --> 01:49:42,184
♪ <i>Till our fingers decompose</i> ♪

2056
01:49:42,358 --> 01:49:49,234
♪ <i>Keep my hand in yours</i> ♪

2057
01:49:53,412 --> 01:49:55,327
♪ <i>Drive slowly</i> ♪

2058
01:49:55,501 --> 01:49:59,549
♪ <i>I know every route</i>
<i>In this county</i> ♪

2059
01:49:59,723 --> 01:50:03,466
♪ <i>Maybe that ain’t</i>
<i>Such a bad thing</i> ♪

2060
01:50:03,640 --> 01:50:06,600
♪ <i>I’ll tell you</i>
<i>Where not to speed</i> ♪

2061
01:50:08,645 --> 01:50:11,430
♪ <i>And it’s been a long year</i> ♪

2062
01:50:11,605 --> 01:50:15,478
♪ <i>And all of our book’s pages </i>
<i>Dog-eared</i> ♪

2063
01:50:15,652 --> 01:50:19,917
♪ <i>We write out the ends</i>
<i>On our palms, dear</i> ♪

2064
01:50:20,091 --> 01:50:22,224
♪ <i>Then forget to read</i> ♪

2065
01:50:24,661 --> 01:50:26,924
♪ <i>We couldn’t know</i> ♪

2066
01:50:27,098 --> 01:50:31,189
♪ <i>That the sun</i>
<i>Was collapsing</i> ♪

2067
01:50:32,713 --> 01:50:35,019
♪ <i>Till the seas rose</i> ♪

2068
01:50:35,193 --> 01:50:39,589
♪ <i>And the buildings</i>
<i>Came crashing</i> ♪

2069
01:50:41,199 --> 01:50:45,639
♪ <i>We cried oh-oh-oh</i>
<i>Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh</i> ♪

2070
01:50:45,813 --> 01:50:48,337
♪ <i>Everywhere, everything</i> ♪

2071
01:50:48,511 --> 01:50:52,254
♪ <i>I wanna love you till we’re </i>
<i>Food for the worms to eat</i> ♪

2072
01:50:52,428 --> 01:50:56,301
♪ <i>Till our fingers decompose</i> ♪

2073
01:50:56,475 --> 01:51:03,439
♪ <i>Keep my hand in yours</i> ♪

2074
01:51:24,286 --> 01:51:26,680
(song ends)